{
	chapter.15B72FB61FF1FB46.subtitle: "Bronze, iron, and steel"
	chapter.15B72FB61FF1FB46.title: "TFC Metalworking"
	chapter.1F2759872355BB36.subtitle: "Planes, trains, and automobiles"
	chapter.1F2759872355BB36.title: "Create: Transportation"
	chapter.7E988D317268FEE5.subtitle: "Steel, oil, and electricity"
	chapter.7E988D317268FEE5.title: "The Factory Must Grow"
	chapter.30E758BE1B4009ED.subtitle: "Real voltage, real current, real resistance"
	chapter.30E758BE1B4009ED.title: "Create: Power Grid"
	chapter.5449CE858435805F.subtitle: "Ore processing, without their own power grid"
	chapter.5449CE858435805F.title: "Mekanism and Immersive Engineering"
	chapter.37EDE754D75D5324.subtitle: "A second forge, a second mine"
	chapter.37EDE754D75D5324.title: "Create Metallurgy"
	chapter.4579E96491254291.subtitle: "From loose rocks to your first metal tools"
	chapter.4579E96491254291.title: "TFC Basics"
	chapter.5EB38D59CA591B1A.subtitle: "First steps"
	chapter.5EB38D59CA591B1A.title: "Getting Started"
	chapter.640FC998E680F1AC.subtitle: "Rotational power, forged not crafted"
	chapter.640FC998E680F1AC.title: "Create Fundamentals"
	chapter_group.0A19049E2EFBBCDC.title: "Industry"
	chapter_group.295D59696748C777.title: "Adventure"
	chapter_group.757B2A0ABFF0DC73.title: "Create and Technology"
	chapter_group.7ECFBA7A9FB006E2.title: "Survival"
	quest.00337C3C1BFC8CC0.quest_desc: ["You've got a rock and a stick - the two ingredients for your first knapped tool. Head into &aTFC Basics&r to actually make it."]
	quest.00337C3C1BFC8CC0.subtitle: "Ready for TFC Basics"
	quest.00337C3C1BFC8CC0.title: "Onward"
	quest.015B09758586B949.quest_desc: [
		"An Ore Vein Atlas (a chest, an amethyst, a map, and a book) records veins you've sampled onto a shareable map."
		""
		"The old Ore Vein Finder isn't craftable in this pack any more - a Prospector's Radar (an ender eye, an amethyst shard, redstone, and two sticks) takes over its exact recipe slot instead. Right-click to open a live radar screen showing every vein within a 16-chunk radius, your current chunk, and the distance to the nearest one; sneak-right-click cycles which vein type it's actually tracking. It has a 3-second cooldown between uses, so it's a tool you check periodically, not one you leave open."
	]
	quest.015B09758586B949.subtitle: "Find a vein before you dig for it"
	quest.015B09758586B949.title: "Scouting Tools"
	quest.017EB16EA61D12AC.quest_desc: ["A Brass Plate and an Electron Tube applied to a regular Borehead Bearing - Simurail's own upgraded version, available once both the Off-Road and Simurail add-ons are loaded together."]
	quest.017EB16EA61D12AC.subtitle: "Where off-road meets rail"
	quest.017EB16EA61D12AC.title: "The Brass Borehead Bearing"
	quest.01D1EB709BDE8400.quest_desc: [
		"Surround a 7-8 layer charcoal pile with 5 stone blocks and light it to convert it into a charcoal forge. It needs a clear line of sight to the sky - directly above, or from one of the 8 blocks around it - to draw air."
		""
		"Five slots on top heat items directly; slots on the side hold vessels and molds that fill automatically as metal melts inside. This is what makes a crucible usable - a firepit alone won't get hot enough."
	]
	quest.01D1EB709BDE8400.subtitle: "A proper heat source"
	quest.01D1EB709BDE8400.title: "The Charcoal Forge"
	quest.04482B9865564E09.quest_desc: ["A Cogwheel, a Block of Industrial Iron, and an Obsidian Plate. Couples simulated train cars together automatically instead of relying on Create's manual Minecart Coupling."]
	quest.04482B9865564E09.subtitle: "Coupling, automated"
	quest.04482B9865564E09.title: "The Automatic Coupler"
	quest.04573090C36BFB97.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an Empty Blaze Burner from netherrack and four iron plates. On its own it's just decoration - right-click a live Blaze with it to capture one, or grab an already-lit burner straight from a spawner in a Nether Fortress, before it's actually useful for industrial heat."
		""
		"Feed it ordinary flammable items to keep it Kindled - the 'heated' state several machines in this book ask for. A Blaze Cake pushes it further, to Seething ('superheated') instead: compact an egg, sugar, and Cinder Flour (ground from netherrack in your Millstone) together in a heated Press and Basin, then fill the result with 250mB of lava. Either state can be fed automatically with a Deployer or Mechanical Arm."
	]
	quest.04573090C36BFB97.subtitle: "A heat source with a mind of its own"
	quest.04573090C36BFB97.title: "The Blaze Burner"
	quest.05366E9B5105E12D.quest_desc: [
		"There's no crafting table. Survival starts with &6knapping&r - shaping loose rocks by hand into your first tools."
		""
		"Hunger is split into five separate nutrition categories instead of one bar, and heat governs cooking, smithing, and working metal. Rock strata determine what ores are nearby, and a real calendar drives the seasons."
		""
		"The next chapter, &aTFC Basics&r, walks through all of this step by step."
	]
	quest.05366E9B5105E12D.subtitle: "No crafting table here"
	quest.05366E9B5105E12D.title: "This Is a TerraFirmaCraft Modpack"
	quest.069C537B7B4C7CFA.quest_desc: ["You've covered the core TFC survival loop: knapping, fire, your first metal, farming, and animals. From here, TFC's own progression continues into bronze, iron, and steel - but the next chapters in this book turn to what makes this specific modpack different, and the technology built on top of TFC."]
	quest.069C537B7B4C7CFA.subtitle: "Core survival, done"
	quest.069C537B7B4C7CFA.title: "Onward"
	quest.0798108559067F59.quest_desc: [
		"Instead of a single hunger bar, your nutrition is tracked across five separate categories: fruit, vegetables, grain, protein, and dairy. Keeping all five topped up raises your maximum health over time; letting them run low lowers it."
		""
		"Food also has an expiration date and will rot if left too long. Storing it in a sealed vessel or large vessel roughly doubles how long it lasts, and salting or pickling extends it even further."
	]
	quest.0798108559067F59.subtitle: "Five categories, not one bar"
	quest.0798108559067F59.title: "Food and Nutrition"
	quest.079B96AEE58F17CE.quest_desc: ["Rails and roads, both covered by the same underlying simulation as the balloons from earlier in this chapter. Combine any of the three and the physics doesn't care which one you're driving."]
	quest.079B96AEE58F17CE.subtitle: "Every way to move, at once"
	quest.079B96AEE58F17CE.title: "Rails and Roads Ready"
	quest.0801144C8E041FB3.quest_desc: [
		"A Cogwheel, a Copper Casing (apply a copper ingot to a stripped log, same as Andesite Casing), and a Sturdy Whisk (Andesite Alloy and a Create sturdy sheet) combine into a Foundry Mixer."
		""
		"Paired with a Foundry running a glassed lid, it does for the Foundry what the Mechanical Mixer does for a Basin - only here, the recipes it runs are real alloys, mixed by exact ratio instead of by hand in a crucible."
	]
	quest.0801144C8E041FB3.subtitle: "Alloying without a crucible"
	quest.0801144C8E041FB3.title: "The Foundry Mixer"
	quest.0AF228B784C923B7.quest_desc: [
		"With Track, Casing, Controls, and a Station in hand, you can build an actual train: open a Station's UI and switch to Assembly Mode, then use Train Casing directly on Track to create bogeys - clicking the track again cycles between bogey designs. Attach the rest of the blocks with Super Glue, place a set of Train Controls somewhere on the structure, and confirm the Assembly from the Station UI."
		""
		"A Wrench relocates an already-assembled train to nearby track. Fuel stored in assembled chests or barrels makes it move faster - fuel kept in a Vault is not consumed."
	]
	quest.0AF228B784C923B7.subtitle: "From blocks to a real train"
	quest.0AF228B784C923B7.title: "Assembling a Train"
	quest.0BFEF82B9646ED4B.quest_desc: ["Bogies, couplers, and gangways - enough to put together a fully physics-simulated train. Simurail is still very early software, so expect rough edges, but the core pieces are all here."]
	quest.0BFEF82B9646ED4B.subtitle: "Trains, the simulated way"
	quest.0BFEF82B9646ED4B.title: "Trains Ready"
	quest.0C47C2CF43D07D11.quest_desc: [
		"Find a raw, unbroken block of igneous rock (granite, diorite, gabbro, basalt, rhyolite, andesite, or dacite) and right-click its exposed top face with any hammer. It instantly becomes an anvil - no crafting recipe needed."
		""
		"A rock anvil is Tier 0, the weakest tier: it can only weld Tier I ingots together, and can't work higher-tier metals at all. It's a stepping stone, but it's what gets you forging."
	]
	quest.0C47C2CF43D07D11.subtitle: "One hammer strike away"
	quest.0C47C2CF43D07D11.title: "The Anvil"
	quest.0D235FE1645713CF.quest_desc: [
		"A Gyroscopic Propeller Bearing works like a regular one, but constantly pitches itself to try to face upward - exactly what a helicopter-style build needs, since a plain Propeller Bearing can't hold that orientation on its own."
		""
		"Mounted facing downward, the same self-righting behavior stabilizes a top-heavy structure instead. A redstone signal resets any built-up tilt back to zero."
	]
	quest.0D235FE1645713CF.subtitle: "A propeller that rights itself"
	quest.0D235FE1645713CF.title: "The Gyroscopic Propeller Bearing"
	quest.0EAE0060AFBFB335.quest_desc: [
		"Mix molten metals in a crucible within these exact ranges - fall outside them and you just get a useless mixture, not an alloy."
		""
		"&6Bronze&r - 88-92% copper, 8-12% tin"
		"&6Bismuth Bronze&r - 50-65% copper, 20-30% zinc, 10-20% bismuth"
		"&6Black Bronze&r - 50-70% copper, 10-25% silver, 10-25% gold"
		""
		"All three reach Tier II on the anvil - a real step up from copper, and the last stop before iron."
	]
	quest.0EAE0060AFBFB335.subtitle: "The real ratios"
	quest.0EAE0060AFBFB335.title: "Bronze and Alloys"
	quest.102ED576775F12ED.quest_desc: [
		"TFC's forge and anvil got you a full metal toolkit by hand. Create builds machines that do that same work for you - rotational power spun up by a water wheel, carried through shafts and cogwheels, and fed into presses, mixers, and mills."
		""
		"This pack runs Create's materials through TFC's own systems, not around them. Andesite Alloy is alloyed and cast like a real metal, and a couple of Create's machines expect genuine TFC forge products - wrought iron double ingots, double sheets - as ingredients instead of Create's plainer originals."
	]
	quest.102ED576775F12ED.subtitle: "Rotation, at last"
	quest.102ED576775F12ED.title: "Welcome to Create"
	quest.1148A71DD1F74CCB.quest_desc: ["A wooden slab, a Gearbox, and a Block of Industrial Iron. Attaches to the block in front of it, reversing incoming rotation and spinning it at a quarter speed - paired with a Storage Container and Rock Cutting Wheels, the whole assembly becomes a moving drill."]
	quest.1148A71DD1F74CCB.subtitle: "A ground-vehicle drill bearing"
	quest.1148A71DD1F74CCB.title: "The Borehead Bearing"
	quest.13A79E259CBF0CFC.quest_desc: [
		"Select a Track, then place a Signal nearby to divide it into segments - only one non-player-driven train is ever allowed into a segment at a time, and a Scheduled train will never cross a signal facing the opposite direction unless a second signal is added facing back the other way."
		""
		"A redstone signal can force one red, and a red signal emits its own comparator output. A wrench switches it to a second, brass-tier mode that also holds a train back if it wouldn't be able to immediately clear the next segment - useful for keeping queued trains out of a busy junction."
	]
	quest.13A79E259CBF0CFC.subtitle: "Keeping trains from colliding"
	quest.13A79E259CBF0CFC.title: "The Track Signal"
	quest.1407308FEBE8B75C.quest_desc: ["Sticks aren't crafted from planks here - find them lying under trees, or craft them from twigs."]
	quest.1407308FEBE8B75C.subtitle: "Not crafted from planks"
	quest.1407308FEBE8B75C.title: "Find a Stick"
	quest.14BA5E52341B0912.quest_desc: ["A scalable alternative to a sign that needs rotational force to run. A written Clipboard gives it static text; a Display Link (from Create's own package network, back in Create Fundamentals) drives dynamic text instead. Individual lines can be dyed, and clicking a line empty-handed resets it."]
	quest.14BA5E52341B0912.subtitle: "A sign that can update itself"
	quest.14BA5E52341B0912.title: "The Display Board"
	quest.16685C33CA1677A2.quest_desc: [
		"An Item Vault and a Transmitter (a lightning rod, three copper plates, and redstone) make a Stock Link. Placing one starts a brand new stock network - right-click an existing Link before placing a second one to join that network instead of starting a separate one."
		""
		"Every Packager linked to that network makes its attached inventory visible and requestable from anywhere else on it. The signal itself has unlimited range; the packages it generates still have to be physically carried, belted, or otherwise moved to wherever they're needed."
	]
	quest.16685C33CA1677A2.subtitle: "One network, every packager on it"
	quest.16685C33CA1677A2.title: "The Stock Link"
	quest.1728460D33D78EA7.quest_desc: [
		"AdventureFirmaCreate is a TerraFirmaCraft-based modpack: realistic, slower-paced survival with some mechanical automation and adventure content layered on top."
		""
		"This quest list covers it chapter by chapter, starting with TFC's survival basics."
	]
	quest.1728460D33D78EA7.subtitle: "Read this first"
	quest.1728460D33D78EA7.title: "Welcome to AdventureFirmaCreate!"
	quest.173DF4E7749FBEC4.quest_desc: [
		"The Whisk this needs isn't crafted either - work a wrought iron double sheet, the same double sheets your blast furnace is built from, at a Tier III anvil, following the rules shown at the top of the interface, to forge one."
		""
		"Combine the Whisk with a Cogwheel and an Andesite Casing for the Mixer itself. Set it above a Basin and it automates any shapeless crafting recipe, plus a handful of recipes unique to Create - some needing a Blaze Burner's heat underneath, same as the Press."
	]
	quest.173DF4E7749FBEC4.subtitle: "One more job for the Tier III anvil"
	quest.173DF4E7749FBEC4.title: "The Mechanical Mixer"
	quest.1C0ACFE74E11A391.quest_desc: [
		"A Shaft plus one plank makes a Cogwheel; a Shaft plus two planks makes a Large Cogwheel. Either can be placed straight onto a shaft, or meshed against another cogwheel to carry rotation sideways."
		""
		"Two meshed cogwheels of the same size spin in opposite directions at the same speed. Mesh a Cogwheel against a Large Cogwheel instead and the smaller one spins twice as fast - your first real gear ratio."
	]
	quest.1C0ACFE74E11A391.subtitle: "Redirect and gear rotation"
	quest.1C0ACFE74E11A391.title: "Cogwheels"
	quest.1DF7CAD92FC96ED4.quest_desc: ["Chains ordinary Minecarts together so they move as a single group - the simple, pre-Train-Contraption way of running more than one cart at once, and still the part Simurail's own Connector is built from."]
	quest.1DF7CAD92FC96ED4.subtitle: "The old way of coupling carts"
	quest.1DF7CAD92FC96ED4.title: "Minecart Coupling"
	quest.1F0A1733E7236B46.quest_desc: [
		"Dig a single 1-block-deep hole and drop up to 4 items into it with the \"V\" button. Cover them with 8 straw (or 2 thatch blocks), then stack 8 logs on top, and light the structure - a torch tossed onto it works just as well as a firestarter."
		""
		"A pit kiln burns for about 6 minutes and reaches up to 1400°C (white heat), hot enough to fire unfired clay into ceramic vessels, or to melt your very first ore without needing a firepit at all."
	]
	quest.1F0A1733E7236B46.subtitle: "No firepit required"
	quest.1F0A1733E7236B46.title: "The Pit Kiln"
	quest.200F0B08D0CD5775.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the base from 3 smooth stone and 3 of any other stone (shaped, smooth on top), and a separate handstone from 3 stones and a wooden rod. Place the base, then right-click its top with the handstone to seat it."
		""
		"Right-click the handstone to load items in, then use the handle on the side to spin it - or shift-click the base to grab the result once it's ground. It's how you get powders (including flux), dyes, and flour. It can also be hooked up to a mechanical power network later, if turning it by hand gets old."
	]
	quest.200F0B08D0CD5775.subtitle: "Grinding, by hand or by power"
	quest.200F0B08D0CD5775.title: "The Quern"
	quest.20C31BA156857A1C.quest_desc: ["Two Andesite Alloy in a vertical line makes 8 Shafts. A shaft on its own does nothing - it only spins once connected to something that generates or relays rotational force, and then it carries that rotation straight through to whatever's on its other end."]
	quest.20C31BA156857A1C.subtitle: "Carries rotation in a straight line"
	quest.20C31BA156857A1C.title: "The Shaft"
	quest.20EB31C3383FC60A.quest_desc: ["Wrench in hand, goggles on, and a mixer running - between your forge and your first machines, there's not much left in early Create that's still out of reach."]
	quest.20EB31C3383FC60A.subtitle: "Configured, measured, and mixing"
	quest.20EB31C3383FC60A.title: "Tooled Up"
	quest.2182667976A60E39.quest_desc: [
		"Collect at least 90mB total of copper ore (native copper, malachite, or tetrahedrite - 9mB from each small ore piece, or more from a full ore chunk) and place it in a small vessel. Heat the vessel in a pit kiln or firepit until the ore fully melts."
		""
		"Pour the molten metal into a fired mold to cast your first tool. Copper is soft and wears out fast compared to later metals, but it's the metal that unlocks proper anvil work."
	]
	quest.2182667976A60E39.subtitle: "TFC's true first metal"
	quest.2182667976A60E39.title: "Smelt Your First Copper"
	quest.21938355214FA1BC.quest_desc: [
		"Working a wrought iron double ingot into a sheet is a Tier III operation - your Tier II bronze anvil can weld wrought iron, but it can't work it. You need the real thing."
		""
		"Weld 7 wrought iron double ingots the same way as before, arrange them in the same 3x3 ring, and you've got a Tier III anvil. This is also the anvil that finally lets you turn those sheets into the double sheets the blast furnace is built from."
	]
	quest.21938355214FA1BC.subtitle: "Tier III - now you can work iron"
	quest.21938355214FA1BC.title: "The Wrought Iron Anvil"
	quest.22487ED0E224B271.quest_desc: [
		"Iron blocks and ingots make an Iron Drill - the actual drill bit you load into a Sample Drill or Drilling Machine to make it run. A Diamond Drill upgrades it further (a diamond block and gems, plus the Iron Drill itself), and a Netherite Drill upgrades that again at a smithing table."
		""
		"Which one you need depends on what you're after. An Iron Drill pulls anything from a common vein - most of TFC's own metals and utility minerals. Uncommon and rare veins (nickel, silver, gold, gems, and TFCM's rarer metals among them) need at least a Diamond Drill. Mithril, the one epic-tier vein in this pack, runs on nothing less than a Netherite Drill."
	]
	quest.22487ED0E224B271.subtitle: "What you'll load into every drill rig"
	quest.22487ED0E224B271.title: "The Iron Drill"
	quest.232F6B7B1E9C80CB.quest_desc: [
		"Wolframite ore melts into Tungsten exactly like any other TFC ore - mine it, heat it past its melting point, and cast it like normal. Create Metallurgy also lists Necromium and Void Steel as alloys, but neither has any usable solid form anywhere in this pack - true dead ends, not worth chasing."
		""
		"Obdurium is the one exception. Mix Andesite Alloy with 60mB of molten Tungsten in a superheated Foundry Mixer for 150mB of molten Obdurium, then cast it at the Casting Table into an ingot or sheet - a real, playable top-tier metal exclusive to this mod."
	]
	quest.232F6B7B1E9C80CB.subtitle: "Create Metallurgy's own top-tier metal"
	quest.232F6B7B1E9C80CB.title: "Tungsten and Obdurium"
	quest.2397E2AD79542E2B.quest_desc: [
		"Between the Foundry and the Drilling Machine, TFC's forge is no longer the only way to turn ore into a finished part - it's just the one you started with."
		""
		"Up next, &aCreate: Aeronautics&r takes rotational power into the sky."
	]
	quest.2397E2AD79542E2B.subtitle: "Two ways to get your metal now"
	quest.2397E2AD79542E2B.title: "Onward"
	quest.25892B48F311E99B.quest_desc: [
		"There are six stone tool heads, each knapped from its own pattern. Combine any head with a stick or twig in a crafting grid to finish the tool - no other ingredients needed."
		""
		"&6Knife&r - harvests straw and plant fiber"
		"&6Axe&r - fells entire trees, logs and leaves both"
		"&6Shovel&r - digs soil and flattens paths"
		"&6Hoe&r - tills farmland, strips leaves"
		"&6Hammer&r - a weak weapon, but the tool you'll swing at anvils"
		"&6Javelin&r - the only stone weapon built for real combat"
		""
		"Durability depends on the rock: sedimentary and metamorphic are the weakest, igneous intrusive is better, and igneous extrusive (basalt, rhyolite, andesite, dacite) makes the toughest stone tools of all."
	]
	quest.25892B48F311E99B.subtitle: "Six heads, one process"
	quest.25892B48F311E99B.title: "Stone Tools"
	quest.258B6E4E1ECA97B7.quest_desc: ["Lift to stay up, thrust to move, and a way to self-stabilize - that's everything a simulated contraption needs to fly under its own control. The rest is building the airframe."]
	quest.258B6E4E1ECA97B7.subtitle: "Ready to fly"
	quest.258B6E4E1ECA97B7.title: "Your First Airship"
	quest.269B0406F099EBBE.quest_desc: ["Simurail is an experimental, early-alpha add-on that replaces a Train Contraption's ordinary bogeys with ones simulated by the same physics engine Aeronautics runs on. An Unpowered Physics Bogie is the base part - Train Casing, Rose Quartz, a Shaft, and steel plates - built from steel here since this pack's own steel ingots fill the tag it checks for."]
	quest.269B0406F099EBBE.subtitle: "A physically simulated wheelset"
	quest.269B0406F099EBBE.title: "Unpowered Physics Bogie"
	quest.271D4A95A007C35D.quest_desc: [
		"Knap an unfired crucible from fire clay, then fire it in a pit kiln or charcoal forge. Set over a lit charcoal forge, it melts down up to 9 items at once and shows the exact percentage of each metal in the mix."
		""
		"Molds and vessels placed on top slowly drain into it too, and it keeps its molten contents even if broken and picked back up - useful for carrying a half-finished alloy somewhere else."
	]
	quest.271D4A95A007C35D.subtitle: "Precision alloying"
	quest.271D4A95A007C35D.title: "The Crucible"
	quest.280C570E6F379BAB.quest_desc: [
		"Small ore pieces lying on the surface only carry about 10mB of metal each on their own, but finding one is a strong sign that a real vein is buried nearby, usually not far underground."
		""
		"Ore only spawns in certain rock types - some metals are tied to igneous rock, others to sedimentary or metamorphic layers - so learning to recognize the stone under your feet will save you a lot of blind digging."
	]
	quest.280C570E6F379BAB.subtitle: "Read the ground"
	quest.280C570E6F379BAB.title: "Prospecting for Ore"
	quest.292780CF7E8DCFFE.quest_desc: [
		"Four Cogwheels around one Andesite Casing makes a Gearbox - a single block that redirects rotation around a corner, instead of stacking multiple cogwheels to do the same thing."
		""
		"A shaft passing straight through comes out reversed; one turning a corner through it comes out mirrored. Worth keeping a few on hand once you start routing power around a build instead of just in a straight line."
	]
	quest.292780CF7E8DCFFE.subtitle: "Turn a corner without the mess"
	quest.292780CF7E8DCFFE.title: "The Gearbox"
	quest.2A1BD732EDE3E72B.quest_desc: [
		"Built from 8 bronze double sheets stacked in layers, each holding 16 items, up to 48 total across three layers. Climb to the top and throw in iron ore and charcoal, then light it and wait 12 minutes."
		""
		"What comes out only melts into cast iron, not wrought iron - it has to be worked at an anvil first into a refined bloom, then worked again into wrought iron ingots. Two full passes, no shortcuts - and it takes at least a Tier II anvil to do it."
	]
	quest.2A1BD732EDE3E72B.subtitle: "Wrought iron, the hard way"
	quest.2A1BD732EDE3E72B.title: "The Bloomery"
	quest.2C2F91E17A717C12.quest_desc: [
		"Seven Andesite Alloy makes a Casting Table. It casts molten metal from the Foundry directly into a finished shape - but not with Create Metallurgy's own Graphite Molds, which this pack disables entirely in favor of Productive Metalworks' Ingot/Nugget/Plate/Rod/Gear Casts instead."
		""
		"A Casting Basin works the same way for bulk block-shaped output instead of a single item. Between the two, this is a full alternative to anvil work for turning fluid metal into a finished part."
	]
	quest.2C2F91E17A717C12.subtitle: "Ingots, sheets, and gears, no anvil needed"
	quest.2C2F91E17A717C12.title: "Casting Table"
	quest.2C60FC8BC3FF74D9.quest_desc: ["A block-mounted Potato Cannon: same ammo as the handheld version, but chargeable with rotational power and fired by a redstone signal once fully charged. Keep the redstone signal held and it fires continuously - and it can be loaded by automated means, not just by hand."]
	quest.2C60FC8BC3FF74D9.subtitle: "The Potato Cannon, mounted"
	quest.2C60FC8BC3FF74D9.title: "The Mounted Potato Cannon"
	quest.32FE41E5C15FEC91.quest_desc: ["Leather stitched onto a pair of Engineer's Goggles. Functionally identical - it augments your HUD with the stress, capacity, and content readouts of whatever kinetic or fluid component you're looking at - just styled for the cockpit instead of the workshop."]
	quest.32FE41E5C15FEC91.subtitle: "The same goggles, restyled"
	quest.32FE41E5C15FEC91.title: "Aviator's Goggles"
	quest.33605436C948E7C5.quest_desc: [
		"Built around a crucible with 8 wrought iron double sheets in a ring, topped with a chimney of reinforced fire bricks - 8 per layer, up to 5 layers, each layer adding 4 more ore capacity."
		""
		"Drop equal parts iron ore and flux down the chimney along with charcoal, place a tuyere in the side, and light it. A bellows attached to any face pushes it past charcoal's usual temperature ceiling - hot enough to melt ore straight into pig iron, which drips down into the crucible below."
	]
	quest.33605436C948E7C5.subtitle: "Steel starts here"
	quest.33605436C948E7C5.title: "The Blast Furnace"
	quest.3414EFD029CB0698.quest_desc: [
		"Put borax, limestone, dolomite, chalk, or marble in your quern and spin the handle to produce flux powder - shells and shellfish remains work too."
		""
		"Without it, you can't weld two pieces of metal together at an anvil, and a blast furnace won't run without it either. Keep a stack on hand at all times."
	]
	quest.3414EFD029CB0698.subtitle: "Needed for welding"
	quest.3414EFD029CB0698.title: "Flux"
	quest.354AFF146A8BD372.quest_desc: [
		"This one isn't made in a crafting grid. Hold an Andesite Alloy and right-click any TFC stripped log or stripped wood with it - every species works - to wrap it in casing instead."
		""
		"Casing shows up as an ingredient in most of Create's actual machines - the Gearbox, Millstone, Mechanical Press, and Mechanical Mixer all need at least one."
	]
	quest.354AFF146A8BD372.subtitle: "Applied, not crafted"
	quest.354AFF146A8BD372.title: "Andesite Casing"
	quest.3902FE60DBE87CEB.quest_desc: ["Loose rocks are scattered on the surface almost everywhere. Pick one up - any type works."]
	quest.3902FE60DBE87CEB.subtitle: "You'll need a few of these"
	quest.3902FE60DBE87CEB.title: "Pick Up a Rock"
	quest.3922605C9E2B98F2.quest_desc: [
		"One Andesite Alloy and TFC's own dried kelp makes 2 Andesite Funnels. Placed normally, a funnel pulls items out of the inventory it's attached to; placed while sneaking, it pushes items in instead - a wrench flips the direction afterward."
		""
		"Redstone power shuts a funnel off entirely. It can't move items directly between two closed inventories or across open air, though - pair it with a belt or a chute for that."
	]
	quest.3922605C9E2B98F2.subtitle: "Extract, insert, automate"
	quest.3922605C9E2B98F2.title: "Andesite Funnels"
	quest.3ABD87425966CCEC.quest_desc: [
		"A genuinely complex build: brass plates, an Electron Tube, a Precision Mechanism, Brass Casing, Create's own Mechanical Drill (Andesite Alloy, Andesite Casing, and an iron ingot - nothing new), and a Sturdy Sheet, all arranged in a 3x3 Mechanical Crafter grid."
		""
		"Place it, load a drill bit, and set a Copper Backtank on top to run it - once it's finished sampling, right-click it with your Ore Vein Atlas to record what it found."
	]
	quest.3ABD87425966CCEC.subtitle: "Test a vein before committing to it"
	quest.3ABD87425966CCEC.title: "Sample Drill"
	quest.3B38FFAB634AEED7.quest_desc: ["A block-mounted version of the same idea: generates thrust when spun, pitches itself upward the same way a Gyroscopic Propeller Bearing does, and reverses thrust with a right-click of the wrench."]
	quest.3B38FFAB634AEED7.subtitle: "The gyroscopic bearing, boxed up"
	quest.3B38FFAB634AEED7.title: "The Smart Propeller"
	quest.3BF8823019D9BEF8.quest_desc: ["A Transmitter, a Quartz gem, and Train Casing. Reads back position and status from a bound Physics Bogie remotely, the counterpart to the Remote Controller's outgoing commands."]
	quest.3BF8823019D9BEF8.subtitle: "Reading a bogie's status"
	quest.3BF8823019D9BEF8.title: "The Bogie Probe Reader"
	quest.3D1CD62F572EE098.quest_desc: ["Andesite Casing, an Iron Sheet, and a Spring (2 Iron Sheets and an Iron Nugget) make a Wheel Mount - it mounts wheel-like items for ground travel, brakes the attached wheel under power from above, and steers it toward whichever side a signal comes from."]
	quest.3D1CD62F572EE098.subtitle: "Where a wheel actually attaches"
	quest.3D1CD62F572EE098.title: "The Wheel Mount"
	quest.3DAB2E63E7003AB9.quest_desc: [
		"Craft one in a 3x3 grid: a row of lumber on top, a row of leather in the middle, a row of lumber on the bottom (6 lumber, 3 leather total). Place it facing a firepit or charcoal forge (one block down also works) and use it."
		""
		"It temporarily raises the device's maximum temperature, at the cost of burning through fuel much faster. Save it for when you actually need the extra heat, not as a default habit."
	]
	quest.3DAB2E63E7003AB9.subtitle: "More heat, more fuel"
	quest.3DAB2E63E7003AB9.title: "The Bellows"
	quest.3E5262DD4D7BFFD4.quest_desc: [
		"Shift+right-click a log to start a log pile, then right-click more logs into it. Bury the pile under soil (or another non-flammable block) and light it - after 15 in-game hours it turns into charcoal, a hotter, cleaner fuel than raw logs."
		""
		"Every device in this chapter burns through it - the charcoal forge, the bloomery, and the blast furnace all need it in bulk, so it's worth stockpiling early."
	]
	quest.3E5262DD4D7BFFD4.subtitle: "Buried and burned"
	quest.3E5262DD4D7BFFD4.title: "Make Charcoal"
	quest.3FF0C57E8478029F.quest_desc: [
		"Regular clay melts before it's any use for serious metalwork. Fire clay can take the heat - made by mixing graphite powder (grind graphite ore in your quern) with kaolinite powder, itself made by heating kaolin clay at only a 20% yield."
		""
		"It's knapped and fired the same way as regular clay, and it's required for crucibles, fire bricks (for the blast furnace), and fire ingot molds, which break far less often than regular ones."
	]
	quest.3FF0C57E8478029F.subtitle: "Clay that can take the heat"
	quest.3FF0C57E8478029F.title: "Fire Clay"
	quest.4083D6FE9F1C293A.quest_desc: ["Fire or steam, you've now got a way to keep a balloon aloft. Either lift source works with the same Envelope Blocks - pick whichever fits the rest of your build."]
	quest.4083D6FE9F1C293A.subtitle: "Two ways to stay up"
	quest.4083D6FE9F1C293A.title: "Lift Systems"
	quest.408C8829BC0702BF.quest_desc: [
		"You can generate, transmit, and use rotational power - the foundation everything else in Create sits on. Later chapters put real numbers on all of it: how much Stress each machine costs to run, how much Capacity each generator provides, and how a whole network balances."
		""
		"The next stop, though, is up - &aCreate: Aeronautics&r covers what this pack builds for getting around and into the sky."
	]
	quest.408C8829BC0702BF.subtitle: "Rotation is only the beginning"
	quest.408C8829BC0702BF.title: "Onward"
	quest.41A1AD445A0D2907.quest_desc: [
		"Not a crafting-grid recipe in this pack - Andesite Alloy is a real TFC alloy. Melt andesite (raw stone or a cut block, either works) at 920°C, then mix the molten rock with tin or zinc in a crucible within one of these ranges:"
		""
		"&6With tin&r - 89-91% andesite, 9-11% tin"
		"&6With zinc&r - 89-91% andesite, 9-11% zinc"
		""
		"Pour 90mB of the finished alloy into a ceramic ingot mold to cast one Andesite Alloy - same crack risk as any other casting. Nearly every early Create block traces back to this one item."
	]
	quest.41A1AD445A0D2907.subtitle: "Alloyed and cast, not crafted"
	quest.41A1AD445A0D2907.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.42B4FE20E7244CCC.quest_desc: ["A Millstone to grind, a Press and Mixer to shape and combine, belts and funnels to move everything between them. That's a complete small processing line - the same handful of parts, arranged differently, scales up into everything Create builds from here."]
	quest.42B4FE20E7244CCC.subtitle: "Untouched by hand, start to finish"
	quest.42B4FE20E7244CCC.title: "Automated Processing"
	quest.454252DFF74FF895.quest_desc: ["A Transmitter, Rose Quartz, and Train Casing - the same Transmitter that starts a Create package network back in Create Fundamentals. Lets a physics train be driven or dispatched from a distance instead of needing a driver seated on board."]
	quest.454252DFF74FF895.subtitle: "Driving from a distance"
	quest.454252DFF74FF895.title: "The Bogie Remote Controller"
	quest.4578F4AA8D02D9BA.quest_desc: [
		"Shift+right-click an animal with its preferred food to raise its familiarity. The more familiar an animal is with you, the more it will let you do - breed it, milk it, shear it, or ride it, depending on the species."
		""
		"Familiarity slowly decays if you stop feeding an animal, so a herd left unattended for too long becomes wild and unmanageable again. Most animals also need to reach adulthood before they're useful for anything beyond meat."
		""
		"Keep a few chickens around and this one takes care of itself - hand in an egg once you've got a coop going."
	]
	quest.4578F4AA8D02D9BA.subtitle: "Feed them, don't neglect them"
	quest.4578F4AA8D02D9BA.title: "Raising Animals"
	quest.46CAA6C7FC2E4FAB.quest_desc: ["Add Brass Plates and a Precision Mechanism to an Unpowered Physics Bogie for a powered one - the version that actually drives a simulated train instead of just rolling along with it."]
	quest.46CAA6C7FC2E4FAB.subtitle: "Now it drives itself"
	quest.46CAA6C7FC2E4FAB.title: "The Physics Bogie"
	quest.46FCAD49663FA8E4.quest_desc: [
		"Two Andesite Alloy, two Andesite Casing, a glass pane, and an Electron Tube make a Storage Terminal. Mount it on the side of an Item Vault (or any other item-holding block) and right-click the screen to open a searchable, sortable view of everything inside."
		""
		"Click an entry to pull a stack, right-click for half, and shift-click to take as much as possible - Deposit All pushes anything in your own inventory that matches back into storage. A terminal not actually touching any storage just warns you, instead of pretending it's looking at an empty vault."
	]
	quest.46FCAD49663FA8E4.subtitle: "Search it instead of digging through it"
	quest.46FCAD49663FA8E4.title: "Storage Terminal"
	quest.471C088B9172D177.quest_desc: [
		"Mix a copper ingot and a zinc ingot in a heated Mechanical Mixer and Basin for 2 Brass Ingots - both metals you already have from TFC. Unlike Andesite Alloy, Brass itself comes out as a real TFC item here, not Create's own."
		""
		"Apply one to a stripped log, the same way you made Andesite Casing, for a Brass Casing (this half stays Create's own item). Brass is the gateway to everything in this chapter's second half - precision components, and the machines Create Ore Excavation builds around them."
	]
	quest.471C088B9172D177.subtitle: "Copper and zinc, mixed and cased"
	quest.471C088B9172D177.title: "Brass"
	quest.47983D2A8A320B99.quest_desc: [
		"Hold clay balls and right-click to open the clay knapping interface - a smaller 4x5 grid, separate from the rock knapping one. Chip away at it the same way, matching the outline of the mold you want (ingot, axe head, knife blade, and so on)."
		""
		"The result is an unfired mold - fragile, and useless until it's been fired. Put it in a firepit or pit kiln and heat it to just under 1400°C to harden it into a real mold, ready to have molten metal poured into it."
	]
	quest.47983D2A8A320B99.subtitle: "Clay knapping, not rock"
	quest.47983D2A8A320B99.title: "Making Molds"
	quest.47FD948BA797E940.quest_desc: ["A Storage Terminal, a Brass Casing, a crafting table, Andesite Alloy, and another Electron Tube upgrade it into a Crafting Storage Terminal - the same search-and-extract interface, but with a crafting grid built in that pulls its ingredients directly from connected storage instead of your own inventory."]
	quest.47FD948BA797E940.subtitle: "Craft straight from what's already stored"
	quest.47FD948BA797E940.title: "Crafting Storage Terminal"
	quest.48335FBE17DB50BF.quest_desc: [
		"Break wild crops you find growing in the world to collect their seeds, then till dirt with a hoe to turn it into farmland before planting."
		""
		"Crops don't strictly need soil nutrients to grow, but Nitrogen, Phosphorous, and Potassium levels in the farmland speed growth and increase yield. Different crop types (cereals, legumes, vegetables, and cover crops) each consume or replenish different nutrients, so rotating what you plant keeps the soil healthy."
	]
	quest.48335FBE17DB50BF.subtitle: "Till, plant, wait"
	quest.48335FBE17DB50BF.title: "Farming"
	quest.48904CEEC0C69260.quest_desc: [
		"Cast pig iron from the blast furnace's crucible into an ingot, then work it at the anvil into high carbon steel, then work that again into a proper steel ingot."
		""
		"Steel comes in four varieties - plain Steel, and the higher tiers Black, Red, and Blue Steel - each of the last three made by alloying a 'weak' version in a crucible first (weak steel is 50-70% steel, 15-25% nickel, 15-25% black bronze), then welding it with pig iron and working it again."
		""
		"Steel itself is Tier IV - you'll need a Tier III (Wrought Iron) anvil just to work it into this ingot in the first place, and a Tier IV anvil, built from steel double ingots, to go any further."
	]
	quest.48904CEEC0C69260.subtitle: "Two anvil passes from pig iron"
	quest.48904CEEC0C69260.title: "Steel"
	quest.4D5EBDD8F45E2B37.quest_desc: [
		"A Stock Link, a gold ingot, and glass make a Stock Ticker. Right-click an existing Stock Link with it before placing it to join that same network, then seat a mob (or place a Blaze Burner) in front of it - that's your Stock Keeper now."
		""
		"Right-click the Keeper to browse everything available across every linked Packager and place an order. Submitted requests get packaged up automatically from wherever they're stored, ready to be carried to wherever you actually need them."
	]
	quest.4D5EBDD8F45E2B37.subtitle: "Order what the network already has"
	quest.4D5EBDD8F45E2B37.title: "The Stock Ticker"
	quest.4E48B5FE94DEB074.quest_desc: [
		"Two iron plates and a wooden barrel make an Item Vault - a high-capacity storage block that holds far more than a chest. Multiple Vaults placed edge to edge merge into one larger inventory, the same way Create's own Fluid Tanks do."
		""
		"There's a catch: nothing can be added or removed from a Vault by hand. Only real item-transfer components - a Funnel, a Belt, a hopper - can actually reach inside one."
	]
	quest.4E48B5FE94DEB074.subtitle: "Storage you can't just walk up to"
	quest.4E48B5FE94DEB074.title: "The Item Vault"
	quest.51A6EE3F7D635DA6.quest_desc: [
		"Five Andesite Alloy in a shaped grid makes a Basin - set one beneath the press before you're done here, since half of what the press does depends on it."
		""
		"The press itself isn't the recipe vanilla Create ships, either: a Shaft, an Andesite Casing, and a wrought iron double ingot - the same double ingot your Tier III anvil is built from - combine into a Mechanical Press."
		""
		"Placed above a Depot, it presses items dropped underneath into sheets one at a time. Placed above the Basin instead, it applies any filled 2x2 or 3x3 crafting recipe to whatever the basin holds - some of those recipes need real heat, supplied by a Blaze Burner underneath (the next quest covers building one)."
	]
	quest.51A6EE3F7D635DA6.subtitle: "Built from your own forge work"
	quest.51A6EE3F7D635DA6.title: "The Mechanical Press"
	quest.521B56616AF187A4.quest_desc: ["Built the same way as a Precision Mechanism back in Metallurgy: run Iron Sheets through 5 loops of Sequenced Assembly - Deploying a Cogwheel, then a Shaft, then a Brass Nugget - before finishing the sequence at a Mechanical Press or Saw."]
	quest.521B56616AF187A4.subtitle: "Another sequenced part"
	quest.521B56616AF187A4.title: "The Gyroscopic Mechanism"
	quest.54153A5A8542998C.quest_desc: ["Right-click any of these onto a Wheel Mount to fit it: the standard Tire, a Small Tire for tighter builds, a Large Tire built around a Belt Connector, and a Monstrous Tire for the biggest ground vehicles. All are built the same way, just from different amounts of dried kelp around a Shaft."]
	quest.54153A5A8542998C.subtitle: "Four sizes of all-terrain wheel"
	quest.54153A5A8542998C.title: "Tires"
	quest.559B64F4FB8A551A.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a Foundry Basin (seven Andesite Alloy and one Refractory Mortar) and a Foundry Lid (five Andesite Alloy) to make a small Foundry - it holds up to 9 items and melts them once you close the lid and heat it with a Blaze Burner underneath."
		""
		"Throw in almost any ordinary TFC metal ingot and it melts down into that same metal as a fluid, ready to be cast into a different shape. A few metals - copper and gold among them - come out as a dead vanilla item instead of anything usable, so don't be surprised if one of those doesn't behave the same way."
	]
	quest.559B64F4FB8A551A.subtitle: "A second furnace, this one automatic"
	quest.559B64F4FB8A551A.title: "The Foundry"
	quest.5626EAFAEEEA82F5.quest_desc: [
		"Create Metallurgy layers a second, parallel line of melting and casting equipment on top of everything you already built - a Foundry that melts any TFC metal ingot directly, and a Casting Table that pours it back out as ingots, sheets, rods, and gears without ever touching an anvil."
		""
		"Create Ore Excavation, covered alongside it here, automates the other half of the job: rotational-power drills that pull ore straight out of the ground once you've found a vein worth mining."
	]
	quest.5626EAFAEEEA82F5.subtitle: "Metal, at industrial scale"
	quest.5626EAFAEEEA82F5.title: "Welcome to Create Metallurgy"
	quest.56807F4C82F6C636.quest_desc: [
		"Crush obsidian into dust, fill it with 500mB of lava, then press it twice for a Sturdy Sheet - Create's own toughened plate material, made with machines you already have."
		""
		"An Electron Tube is simpler: stack polished rose quartz on an iron plate. Both feed straight into the Sample Drill and the Drilling Machine itself."
	]
	quest.56807F4C82F6C636.subtitle: "Two pieces every drill rig needs"
	quest.56807F4C82F6C636.title: "Small Parts"
	quest.56B97A7FB0A90AC5.quest_desc: [
		"A Cogwheel, an Andesite Casing, and any TFC stone, stacked vertically, makes a Millstone. Power it from the side with a shaft or cogwheel, then throw or insert items in the top - after a short delay, right-click it to collect the ground result."
		""
		"It only ever gives one output per item processed. A proper pair of Crushing Wheels - a later, more advanced build - grinds faster and adds a chance at a bonus second output, which matters a lot once you start running ore through it."
	]
	quest.56B97A7FB0A90AC5.subtitle: "Your first machine"
	quest.56B97A7FB0A90AC5.title: "The Millstone"
	quest.5848C4CB9355FB4C.quest_desc: [
		"A Steam Vent does the same job as a Hot Air Burner - filling the balloon above it on a redstone signal - but runs on steam instead of fire, needing the same heat, water, and boiler space a Steam Engine does."
		""
		"Same rule applies: the Envelope's size caps how much lift you get, and several vents can combine their output into one balloon."
	]
	quest.5848C4CB9355FB4C.subtitle: "Lift from steam"
	quest.5848C4CB9355FB4C.title: "The Steam Vent"
	quest.58697FF2B344CB6D.quest_desc: ["Track, a station, signals, and a way to schedule or drive a train - Create's own rail system is now fully in reach. Simurail builds a physically-simulated upgrade directly on top of it."]
	quest.58697FF2B344CB6D.subtitle: "Create's own trains, covered"
	quest.58697FF2B344CB6D.title: "Rolling Stock"
	quest.590B1AF9CF260033.quest_desc: ["Train Casing, an Electron Tube, and a Crushing Wheel. An optional attachment for a simulated train's undercarriage."]
	quest.590B1AF9CF260033.subtitle: "An extra undercarriage part"
	quest.590B1AF9CF260033.title: "The Physics Roller"
	quest.593E306E3C713CD0.quest_desc: ["Select a Track, then place an Observer nearby - it detects any train passing the marker, and can be filtered to trigger only for specific cargo."]
	quest.593E306E3C713CD0.subtitle: "Detecting a passing train"
	quest.593E306E3C713CD0.title: "The Track Observer"
	quest.5987DA3762DA7D0A.quest_desc: [
		"An Envelope Block encloses a volume that generates lift once it's filled with hot air - hot air fills a balloon from the top down, and needs to stay contained by airtight blocks to work. Shafts can be encased in Envelope Blocks to pass rotation through the balloon without breaking that seal."
		""
		"Envelopes come in all 16 dye colors - right-click one with a dye to repaint it, or wash it back to white in a Water Wheel or Basin under running water."
	]
	quest.5987DA3762DA7D0A.subtitle: "The balloon itself"
	quest.5987DA3762DA7D0A.title: "Envelope Blocks"
	quest.5BEF08AD5D95D444.quest_desc: ["Select a Train Track, then place a Station nearby - Stations are the waypoints of the whole track network, and the only place a Train Contraption can be assembled or disassembled back into blocks. Using a map on one adds a labeled marker at its location."]
	quest.5BEF08AD5D95D444.subtitle: "A waypoint on the network"
	quest.5BEF08AD5D95D444.title: "The Train Station"
	quest.5D31A5DC1A983003.quest_desc: [
		"Both of these route through the Mechanical Press you just built. Press a gold ingot into a Golden Sheet first, then:"
		""
		"&6Wrench&r - 3 Golden Sheets, a Cogwheel, and a TFC twig. Right-click most Create blocks with it to rotate or reconfigure them, shift-right-click to pick one back up whole instead of breaking it."
		""
		"&6Goggles&r - a Golden Sheet, TFC wool yarn, and glass. Wear them and look at any spinning shaft, cogwheel, or machine to read its exact RPM and Stress Unit values on screen."
	]
	quest.5D31A5DC1A983003.subtitle: "Now that the press is running"
	quest.5D31A5DC1A983003.title: "Wrench and Goggles"
	quest.5F653C1992AF5BC2.quest_desc: [
		"Every quest here is a task - some are simple checkmarks, others ask you to hand in a specific item. Completing one usually grants a reward, claimable from its reward icon."
		""
		"Chapters are listed in the tabs on the side. Some quests depend on others and won't unlock until the one before them is done."
	]
	quest.5F653C1992AF5BC2.subtitle: "How this book works"
	quest.5F653C1992AF5BC2.title: "Using This Quest List"
	quest.5FA57DC42371202C.quest_desc: ["Between a working drill bit and the tools to find where to point it, there's nothing left stopping you from setting up your first automated dig site."]
	quest.5FA57DC42371202C.subtitle: "Scouted and equipped"
	quest.5FA57DC42371202C.title: "Ready to Dig"
	quest.6150FE87C0034D10.quest_desc: ["Two Obsidian Plates around a Minecart Coupling. Simurail's own coupler item, built from the same coupling Create's ordinary minecarts already use."]
	quest.6150FE87C0034D10.subtitle: "Simurail's own coupler"
	quest.6150FE87C0034D10.title: "The Bogie Connector"
	quest.62567FA6CD2EAFD5.quest_desc: [
		"Hold at least two rocks of the same rock category (sedimentary, metamorphic, igneous intrusive, or igneous extrusive) and right-click in the air to open the knapping interface. It's a 5x5 grid, fully filled in with stone at the start."
		""
		"Click individual squares to chip them away. You're not filling in a shape, you're removing everything that isn't part of it - clear squares away until what remains matches one of the known tool head patterns. The pattern's position on the grid doesn't matter, and several tools accept more than one valid arrangement, so there's some room for error."
		""
		"Knapping consumes one of the two rocks and produces one tool head if the shape is right. This chapter will get you through your first axe and knife, but the same process makes every stone tool head in the game."
	]
	quest.62567FA6CD2EAFD5.subtitle: "Two rocks, one tool head"
	quest.62567FA6CD2EAFD5.title: "Knapping Your First Tool"
	quest.6262E5A58142DF2A.quest_desc: ["Required on board every Train Contraption. Right-click to start driving - movement keys accelerate and steer, and the mouse wheel fine-tunes the top speed. Hold space to pull into a nearby Station, and sneak or click again to stop driving. A second set lets a train depart a Station in either direction."]
	quest.6262E5A58142DF2A.subtitle: "Actually driving the thing"
	quest.6262E5A58142DF2A.title: "Train Controls"
	quest.62C6C4097E0593FD.quest_desc: [
		"This pack's Precision Mechanism skips Create's usual brass-heavy recipe entirely. Starting from a TFC gold sheet, deploy a Cogwheel onto it, then Brass Mechanisms (press a heated Brass Ingot in a Basin for 2), then a wrought iron rod straight off your anvil - run that whole sequence twice to finish it."
		""
		"Everything here except the Brass Mechanisms step is something you already know how to make from TFC alone."
	]
	quest.62C6C4097E0593FD.subtitle: "Built from the forge, not from brass"
	quest.62C6C4097E0593FD.title: "Precision Mechanism"
	quest.64E91DEEC8FD6960.quest_desc: ["A Crushing Wheel, a Block of Industrial Iron, and an Iron Sheet. Unlike a regular drill, Rock Cutting Wheels break every block in a range around themselves, and attach to other blocks and each other automatically - no Super Glue needed. Mining speed depends on the rotation fed in, and more Borehead Bearings offset the slowdown from cutting more blocks at once."]
	quest.64E91DEEC8FD6960.subtitle: "Digging as you drive"
	quest.64E91DEEC8FD6960.title: "The Rock Cutting Wheel"
	quest.64F1DD5A3CC0997E.quest_desc: ["Placed on a Fluid Tank that's holding enough heat, a Steam Whistle plays a note when activated - a Whistle item lowers its pitch, and a wrench cycles between three octaves. An assembled Whistle on a moving train can be sounded with the sprint key while driving."]
	quest.64F1DD5A3CC0997E.subtitle: "Every train needs one"
	quest.64F1DD5A3CC0997E.title: "The Steam Whistle"
	quest.67F91A01E4432163.quest_desc: [
		"Bronze is Tier II, so weld two bronze ingots together (flux, heat, hammer, same as before) into a double ingot, seven times over. You'll need your Tier I copper anvil to do the welding - a Tier N anvil welds Tier N+1, and it can't skip a step."
		""
		"Arrange the 7 double ingots in the same 3x3 ring as before and you've got a Tier II anvil - now you can both work and weld bronze, and you're one weld away from working with iron."
	]
	quest.67F91A01E4432163.subtitle: "Tier II - the last stop before iron"
	quest.67F91A01E4432163.title: "The Bronze Anvil"
	quest.68B3523C5F0761AF.quest_desc: [
		"Start from Deepslate Bricks, apply Refractory Mortar, then an Obdurium Sheet, grind it down, and fill it with 30mB of molten Tungsten to finish an Industrial Crucible - a full sequenced-assembly build, not a simple crafting recipe."
		""
		"Multiple Crucibles placed edge to edge merge into one larger structure, the same way Create's own Fluid Tanks do. A 5x5 footprint reaches maximum temperature, but only if every block in that footprint has its own Blaze Burner underneath - skip one and the whole structure runs cooler."
	]
	quest.68B3523C5F0761AF.subtitle: "The Foundry's big brother"
	quest.68B3523C5F0761AF.title: "Industrial Crucible"
	quest.694680A9A7D620D0.quest_desc: ["Wheels to roll on and a bearing to dig with - everything for a ground vehicle that can drive itself over rough terrain, on the same simulated physics as everything else in this chapter."]
	quest.694680A9A7D620D0.subtitle: "Wheels on the ground"
	quest.694680A9A7D620D0.title: "Off-Road Ready"
	quest.6A42CAE76F6E20A4.quest_desc: [
		"A Propeller Bearing attaches to whatever structure is built directly in front of it - any arrangement of at least 2 sail-like blocks counts as a valid propeller, and more sails mean more thrust."
		""
		"Spinning the bearing produces thrust that can push a contraption through the air; a wrench reverses the direction. Thrust drops off both at higher airspeeds and at higher altitude, where the air thins out."
	]
	quest.6A42CAE76F6E20A4.subtitle: "Thrust, not lift"
	quest.6A42CAE76F6E20A4.title: "The Propeller Bearing"
	quest.6BC40AEBBFCB5CC1.quest_desc: [
		"Six of TFC's own dried kelp makes one Belt Connector. It isn't placed like a normal block - right-click one shaft with it, then right-click a second shaft between 2 and 20 blocks away, and a belt stretches between them."
		""
		"Both shafts then spin at identical speed and direction. The belt itself carries any item or entity dropped or placed on top of it, making it the main way to physically move things between your machines."
	]
	quest.6BC40AEBBFCB5CC1.subtitle: "Not a block, an item"
	quest.6BC40AEBBFCB5CC1.title: "Mechanical Belts"
	quest.6C6BD602F494DF36.quest_desc: ["Deploy an Obsidian Plate onto a Brass Casing for Train Casing - the base material behind almost every block in this section, from bogeys to stations to signals."]
	quest.6C6BD602F494DF36.subtitle: "The material behind the railway"
	quest.6C6BD602F494DF36.title: "Train Casing"
	quest.6CC22697BC6007E0.quest_desc: ["Melting, alloying, casting, and moving fluid metal by hand or by ladle - the Foundry line covers the same ground TFC's forge does, just automated and running in parallel to it."]
	quest.6CC22697BC6007E0.subtitle: "Every piece, working together"
	quest.6CC22697BC6007E0.title: "The Complete Foundry"
	quest.6CDECBA71D5AC615.quest_desc: [
		"A new type of rail built for Train Contraptions, not regular minecarts. Click an existing track and then place or select a second point to connect a whole row at once - hold sprint while connecting for the longest fitting bend instead of the tightest one. Tracks can be laid as turns or slopes, and whatever's in your off-hand gets paved underneath them automatically."
		""
		"Made the same way as a Precision Mechanism: Sequenced Assembly on a stone or andesite slab, deploying iron or zinc nuggets twice, then a final Pressing pass."
	]
	quest.6CDECBA71D5AC615.subtitle: "Rails for real trains"
	quest.6CDECBA71D5AC615.title: "Train Track"
	quest.6FD8E7AE6E6238D0.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a Schedule to program a destination, then hand it to a driver - any mob or Blaze Burner seated in front of a train's Controls counts, and a leashed creature can be given its seat directly. A programmed train then runs itself; the Schedule can be retrieved from its driver at any time."
		""
		"Placed on a Station instead, a Schedule copies itself automatically to any train that stops there - unlike handing one to a driver directly, the train won't carry that copy away with it."
	]
	quest.6FD8E7AE6E6238D0.subtitle: "Letting a train drive itself"
	quest.6FD8E7AE6E6238D0.title: "The Schedule"
	quest.6FE0BC29D1E4B6F0.quest_desc: ["Planes, trains, and automobiles - all three now covered, all three built on the same underlying physics simulation. A few more add-ons build on top of what's here: fold-space warp drives for airships, drive-by-wire controls, a tool gun that can pack up and redeploy whole vehicles, cannon ballistics radar, and dedicated airship/train dispatch stations - worth exploring later if you want to take any of this further."]
	quest.6FE0BC29D1E4B6F0.subtitle: "Every way to get around"
	quest.6FE0BC29D1E4B6F0.title: "Onward"
	quest.6FE7A8A4ADD116C7.quest_desc: ["You can now go from raw ore to a finished steel tool without ever touching a crafting table. The next chapters turn to Create and the rest of the technology built on top of everything you've just learned."]
	quest.6FE7A8A4ADD116C7.subtitle: "The forge is yours"
	quest.6FE7A8A4ADD116C7.title: "Onward"
	quest.701DE07BF684DEA8.quest_desc: ["Mix 4 End Stone Powder (crushed from End Stone) and 2 Zinc Nuggets into 500mB of water, heated, for Levitite Blend - the raw, uncrystallized form of this chapter's anti-gravity material."]
	quest.701DE07BF684DEA8.subtitle: "Raw anti-gravity, sort of"
	quest.701DE07BF684DEA8.title: "Levitite Blend"
	quest.729A379F32BA554C.quest_desc: [
		"Bring a heat source near Levitite Blend and it starts crystallizing into solid Levitite - once started, the reaction spreads through the whole fluid on its own, and there's no undoing it back into Blend."
		""
		"Enough Levitite attached to a contraption keeps it floating in place - it won't gain altitude on Levitite alone, since it actually resists motion at low speed (that resistance drops off at higher speed), but it's a steady hover with no burner or vent required. Blocks tagged as breaking on crystallization can be used to cast Levitite into specific shapes."
	]
	quest.729A379F32BA554C.subtitle: "Where the hovering happens"
	quest.729A379F32BA554C.title: "Levitite"
	quest.7466D020492F80B8.quest_desc: ["Lift and thrust both weaken as altitude increases, since the air gets thinner. An Altitude Sensor reads the exact air pressure at its position, so a redstone contraption can react to it directly instead of guessing."]
	quest.7466D020492F80B8.subtitle: "Reading the air"
	quest.7466D020492F80B8.title: "The Altitude Sensor"
	quest.755332AA752A98DB.quest_desc: [
		"Every anvil has a tier, and the rule never changes: it can work metals at its own tier, and weld metals one tier higher. Your rock anvil is Tier 0, so it can weld Tier I - copper - but it can't work copper at all."
		""
		"&6Tier 0&r - Rock &6Tier I&r - Copper &6Tier II&r - Bronze family &6Tier III&r - Wrought Iron &6Tier IV&r - Steel &6Tier V&r - Black Steel &6Tier VI&r - Red/Blue Steel"
		""
		"Weld two copper ingots with flux into a double ingot, seven times over, then arrange them in a 3x3 crafting grid (a ring of 7 with the corners and middle empty) to get your first metal anvil. From here you can both work AND weld copper - and you'll need to repeat this same double-ingot upgrade at every tier from here on."
		""
		"Working an item means lining up a progress bar with a hammer, following the rules shown at the top of the interface. Do it well and the result comes out Poorly, Well, Expertly, or Perfectly Forged, each step boosting durability, speed, or damage."
	]
	quest.755332AA752A98DB.subtitle: "Tier I - work at last"
	quest.755332AA752A98DB.title: "The Copper Anvil"
	quest.75557EDA9E07C0E7.quest_desc: [
		"Powered by redstone, a Hot Air Burner gradually fills the Envelope above it with hot air - its input panel sets a maximum output, and the redstone signal strength scales that output proportionally. Multiple burners can feed a single balloon for more lift."
		""
		"The lift a burner can produce is capped by how big the balloon actually is, so bigger envelopes are not just for looks."
	]
	quest.75557EDA9E07C0E7.subtitle: "Lift from fire"
	quest.75557EDA9E07C0E7.title: "The Hot Air Burner"
	quest.75C04C84220A2CA2.quest_desc: [
		"Throw a log, 3 sticks, and up to 5 kindling items (straw, paper, or pinecones - each one adds roughly +10% success chance) onto the same block. Craft a firestarter from two sticks, then hold right-click on the pile with it until smoke, then fire, appears."
		""
		"A lit firepit has four fuel slots (logs, peat, or stick bundles) and a temperature gauge. Use it to cook raw food and doughs, turn sticks into torches, and - once it's hot enough - melt your first bits of metal."
	]
	quest.75C04C84220A2CA2.subtitle: "Your first real heat source"
	quest.75C04C84220A2CA2.title: "Build a Firepit"
	quest.77AE9D3D84D06910.quest_desc: ["A Shaft in the center of a 3x3 of planks makes a Water Wheel. Place it so its blades face flowing water and it generates rotational force on its own, no fuel or player input needed - a later chapter covers exactly how much power it, and everything else that generates it, actually produces."]
	quest.77AE9D3D84D06910.subtitle: "Your first source of power"
	quest.77AE9D3D84D06910.title: "The Water Wheel"
	quest.78321E0C66E146B5.quest_desc: [
		"Clay hides underground, but it always gives itself away on the surface: look for &6athyrium fern, canna, goldenrod, pampas grass, perovskia, or water canna&r growing nearby. Wherever you see one of these, there's a clay patch under the grass close by."
		""
		"Dig into the patch (any shovel works, even the stone one) to break it apart - each block gives 1-3 clay balls. Grab a stack; you'll go through more of it than you'd expect, between vessels, molds, and later pottery."
	]
	quest.78321E0C66E146B5.subtitle: "Follow the plants"
	quest.78321E0C66E146B5.title: "Finding Clay"
	quest.7AFA0763108AE957.quest_desc: [
		"The real thing: the same family of parts as the Sample Drill, just more of them, arranged in a full 5x5 Mechanical Crafter grid. Load a drill bit and power it with rotational force, and it pulls ore directly from whichever vein occupies that chunk - no mining required."
		""
		"Every vein this pack adds is infinite and ignores TFC's own rock layers entirely. A Fluid Well Extractor exists too, built the same way, but only water veins are active in this pack, so it's a minor curiosity rather than something worth chasing."
	]
	quest.7AFA0763108AE957.subtitle: "Rotational force does the digging"
	quest.7AFA0763108AE957.title: "The Drilling Machine"
	quest.7B3513914F95C9E8.quest_desc: [
		"A Transfer Ladle (a small sequenced-assembly item, with several cosmetic variants) scoops fluid straight out of a Foundry or Crucible and carries it by hand to wherever you pour it back out - no pump or fluid pipe required for small jobs."
		""
		"A Labeling Station writes an address onto a ladle held back by redstone power, using whatever lines starting with '#' are on an attached clipboard - a way to sort automated ladle traffic by destination once you're running more than one at a time."
	]
	quest.7B3513914F95C9E8.subtitle: "Move fluid metal without a pipe"
	quest.7B3513914F95C9E8.title: "The Transfer Ladle"
	quest.7C2B403E913EC9D2.quest_desc: [
		"Rotational power built machines; brass and precision mechanisms built Metallurgy's finer tools. Aeronautics turns both toward a new problem: getting off the ground."
		""
		"Everything here is built from Create parts you already know - brass casing, andesite alloy, iron sheets - plus a handful of new materials this chapter introduces along the way."
	]
	quest.7C2B403E913EC9D2.subtitle: "Getting off the ground"
	quest.7C2B403E913EC9D2.title: "Welcome to Create: Aeronautics"
	quest.7EBB0197C5BE0EF7.quest_desc: ["That covers flight: lift, thrust, and a way to self-stabilize is everything a balloon needs to fly under its own control. Trains and cars run on the same underlying physics - next up."]
	quest.7EBB0197C5BE0EF7.subtitle: "Flight, covered"
	quest.7EBB0197C5BE0EF7.title: "Aircraft Ready"
	quest.7F72C06FA326C8A5.quest_desc: [
		"Mix four pulpifiable items (bamboo, or any tree sapling) with 250mB of water in a heated Basin and Mixer for Pulp, then press it into Cardboard - four Cardboard makes a Cardboard Block."
		""
		"Combine that with iron ingots and redstone for a Packager. Attach it to the side of an inventory and give it redstone power, and it boxes that inventory's contents into a Package - a real item you can carry, drop on a belt, or feed into another Packager to unpack again. Write a sign on top first and every package it makes carries that text as an address."
	]
	quest.7F72C06FA326C8A5.subtitle: "Boxing up whatever's in an inventory"
	quest.7F72C06FA326C8A5.title: "The Packager"
	quest.7FCCF25953A60E02.quest_desc: ["A Block of Industrial Iron and two Obsidian Plates make 4 Gangway Frames - the connecting corridor pieces that link simulated train cars into one continuous structure, in the many angled and offset shapes a real train needs."]
	quest.7FCCF25953A60E02.subtitle: "Walking between cars"
	quest.7FCCF25953A60E02.title: "The Gangway Frame"

	quest.690239F4E1A94E03.quest_desc: [
		"Metallurgy's brass and precision mechanisms unlocked Create's finer machines. This add-on builds a whole second industrial tier on top of that: oil drilled and refined into fuel and plastic, generated electricity, and printed circuit boards."
		""
		"One thing is different from the mod's own tutorial: in this pack, Cast Iron and Steel are TFC's own - the same Cast Iron Ingot and Steel Ingot your Metalworking already produces. This add-on's own Blast Furnace still exists and is worth building, but its real payoff here is Silicon, not metal you already have."
	]
	quest.690239F4E1A94E03.subtitle: "Steel and cast iron, already in hand"
	quest.690239F4E1A94E03.title: "Welcome to The Factory Must Grow"
	quest.569FB7E5F377BD86.quest_desc: ["Smelt a Fire Clay - the same one from Metalworking - in a regular furnace for a Fireproof Brick, then craft 4 of those together for Fireproof Bricks. It's the only material that can survive lining a working Blast Furnace or Chemical Vat."]
	quest.569FB7E5F377BD86.subtitle: "Fire Clay, put to a new use"
	quest.569FB7E5F377BD86.title: "Fireproof Bricks"
	quest.128833CEF75A5520.quest_desc: [
		"Coal goes in, Coal Coke comes out - slowly, so it's worth running several Coke Ovens side by side. Coal can be inserted from anywhere; Carbon Dioxide vents from the top and Creosote can be drawn from any other side."
		""
		"Creosote (and Furnace Gas, a byproduct of actually running the Blast Furnace) are exactly what a Blast Stove burns for fuel - this add-on's first closed loop."
	]
	quest.128833CEF75A5520.subtitle: "Slow, but worth arraying"
	quest.128833CEF75A5520.title: "The Coke Oven"
	quest.20A15AA866AB30BE.quest_desc: [
		"Pump fuel (Creosote or Furnace Gas) into the bottom and air into the side, and a Blast Stove produces Hot Air out the top - the heat source a Blast Furnace runs on."
		""
		"It also produces Carbon Dioxide as it runs, which will stall the process if it isn't vented - build a Smokestack or Exhaust nearby to keep it running."
	]
	quest.20A15AA866AB30BE.subtitle: "Turning fuel and air into hot air"
	quest.20A15AA866AB30BE.title: "The Blast Stove"
	quest.7322B17969B6D21C.quest_desc: [
		"Ring a Blast Furnace Output with Fireproof Bricks, set one Blast Furnace Hatch into that ring as the Hot Air input, and add Blast Furnace Reinforcements around the outside to speed it up. Feed it from a hole in the top."
		""
		"In stock TFMG this multiblock makes Steel - but this pack already gives you Steel and Cast Iron straight from TFC's own Blast Furnace, so don't bother feeding it crushed iron. Its real job here shows up later in this chapter: fed Quartz instead, the exact same structure produces Liquid Silicon for circuit boards."
	]
	quest.7322B17969B6D21C.subtitle: "Worth building, for what comes later"
	quest.7322B17969B6D21C.title: "The Blast Furnace"
	quest.3EBDB1B02D913C8D.quest_desc: ["Steel Cogwheels and Large Steel Cogwheels are simple ingot-plus-shaft crafts, made straight from the Steel Ingots you already have. Steel Casing is applied by hand: deploy a Steel Ingot onto Hardened Planks, the same way Brass Casing goes onto a stripped log back in Metallurgy."]
	quest.3EBDB1B02D913C8D.subtitle: "Brass parts, but steel"
	quest.3EBDB1B02D913C8D.title: "Steel-Tier Kinetics"
	quest.3DBEF6700140548A.quest_desc: ["Apply a Steel Plate to a block of Steel Casing for Heavy Machinery Casing - from here on, almost every machine in this add-on is built around this one block."]
	quest.3DBEF6700140548A.subtitle: "The casing behind everything industrial"
	quest.3DBEF6700140548A.title: "Heavy Machinery Casing"
	quest.4D66D931F9F3CAA7.quest_desc: ["Built the same way as Metallurgy's Precision Mechanism: run a Steel Sheet through Sequenced Assembly, deploying a Steel Cogwheel, a Nickel Sheet, a Large Steel Cogwheel, a Lead Sheet, a Screw, and a Screwdriver, for 2 full loops. All the sheets here are real TFC and TFCM metal, pressed the same way as any other - not a separate material this add-on introduces on its own."]
	quest.4D66D931F9F3CAA7.subtitle: "This add-on's Precision Mechanism"
	quest.4D66D931F9F3CAA7.title: "The Steel Mechanism"
	quest.196248DBF5923552.quest_desc: ["A ring of Steel Cogwheels around a Heavy Machinery Casing - the steel-tier answer to Create's own Gearbox."]
	quest.196248DBF5923552.subtitle: "Redirecting steel-tier rotation"
	quest.196248DBF5923552.title: "The Steel Gearbox"
	quest.10B72D484823918E.quest_desc: ["A Blast Furnace built (even if its metal output goes unused for now) and a full set of steel-tier casings and mechanisms - the foundation everything else in this chapter runs on."]
	quest.10B72D484823918E.subtitle: "A furnace built, a toolkit assembled"
	quest.10B72D484823918E.title: "The Steel Age"
	quest.1648763B5CB1919A.quest_desc: ["Powered from below by a Machine Input, a Surface Scanner lights up a 5x5 grid of surrounding chunks - any chunk that glows has at least one Oil Deposit in it. No glow within a few seconds usually means there's nothing nearby. F3+G shows chunk borders in-world if you need to line it up."]
	quest.1648763B5CB1919A.subtitle: "Finding oil before you dig"
	quest.1648763B5CB1919A.title: "The Surface Scanner"
	quest.0F4AD82C6B04E45C.quest_desc: ["Run Industrial Pipes down from an Oil Deposit to the surface, place a Pumpjack Base on top facing away from where the Hammer Holder will sit, and build the Hammer Holder, Connector, and Head above a Pumpjack Crank - all Super Glued together. A Machine Input above the crank provides the rotational power that drives the whole assembly, pumping up Crude Oil."]
	quest.0F4AD82C6B04E45C.subtitle: "Drilling for crude oil"
	quest.0F4AD82C6B04E45C.title: "The Pumpjack"
	quest.19ED4EC34E12C53F.quest_desc: [
		"Stack Steel Fluid Tanks, attach a Steel Distillation Controller to feed crude oil in, and surround the tower with up to 6 Steel Distillation Outputs linked by Industrial Pipes. A heat source underneath powers it - the dial on the tower shows its current power level, and how many outputs you've actually built changes which fuel fractions come out."
		""
		"A fully-built, fully-heated tower splits crude oil into Heavy Oil, Diesel, Kerosene, Naphtha, Gasoline, and LPG all at once; fewer outputs or less heat collapses some of those fractions together instead."
	]
	quest.19ED4EC34E12C53F.subtitle: "Cracking crude oil into fuels"
	quest.19ED4EC34E12C53F.title: "The Distillation Tower"
	quest.31D978B715AB2280.quest_desc: ["A working Pumpjack and a Distillation Tower - crude oil is no longer just a fluid in the ground, it's Diesel, Gasoline, Naphtha, and everything downstream of them."]
	quest.31D978B715AB2280.subtitle: "From crude to usable fuel"
	quest.31D978B715AB2280.title: "Striking Oil"
	quest.6298334B7A0A299E.quest_desc: ["Fireproof Bricks, Cast Iron Plates, and a Cast Iron Pipe make a Casting Basin. Its stock job is casting metal ingots, but you already have Steel and Cast Iron from TFC - here it's for casting Plastic Sheets, and later, Silicon Ingots."]
	quest.6298334B7A0A299E.subtitle: "Not for metal, this time"
	quest.6298334B7A0A299E.title: "The Casting Basin"
	quest.5F0D5361C63A348E.quest_desc: ["A Chemical Vat is a plain casing until you attach something to it. Insert an Industrial Mixer's Mixer Blade and it becomes a Mixer capable of the recipes in this section; other attachments turn the same vat into an Electrolyzer (2 Electrode Holders) or an Electric Arc Furnace (3 Graphite Electrodes)."]
	quest.5F0D5361C63A348E.subtitle: "One machine, many uses"
	quest.5F0D5361C63A348E.title: "The Chemical Vat"
	quest.178078BB0247A7CD.quest_desc: ["In a heated Chemical Vat fitted as a Mixer, Naphtha cracks into Ethylene and Propylene; either one, mixed again with heat, becomes Molten Plastic. Cast that in your Casting Basin for Plastic Sheets - the material behind circuit boards, resistors, transistors, and synthetic everything."]
	quest.178078BB0247A7CD.subtitle: "Naphtha, cracked and cast"
	quest.178078BB0247A7CD.title: "Plastic"
	quest.10FD72A2934883C1.quest_desc: ["Sulfur Dust and Heavy Oil, mixed with heat in a Chemical Vat, produce a Rubber Sheet directly - no intermediate fluid needed. A genuinely optional side-product; nothing later in this chapter requires it."]
	quest.10FD72A2934883C1.subtitle: "Sulfur and heavy oil"
	quest.10FD72A2934883C1.title: "Rubber"
	quest.03FD75D29220A5FF.quest_desc: ["Sulfur Dust, Nitrate Dust, and water mixed in a Chemical Vat produce Sulfuric Acid - unglamorous now, but it's exactly what an Etched Circuit Board is bathed in further down this chapter."]
	quest.03FD75D29220A5FF.subtitle: "For etching, later"
	quest.03FD75D29220A5FF.title: "Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.135E0001D267273D.quest_desc: ["Heavy Oil, heated in a Mixer, compacts into Bitumen. Mix that with sand and gravel (or Slag and gravel, for double the yield) for Asphalt Mixture, then mix that with water for Liquid Asphalt to pave with. This one skips the Chemical Vat entirely - it's a plain Mechanical Mixer recipe, and entirely optional."]
	quest.135E0001D267273D.subtitle: "Paving the factory floor"
	quest.135E0001D267273D.title: "Asphalt"
	quest.0A41C516E73C9C7C.quest_desc: ["Aluminum isn't smelted here - it's electrolyzed, the same way TFC/TFCM makes it. Fit a Chemical Vat with 2 Electrode Holders and copper electrodes to make an Electrolyzer, then feed it Bauxite Powder for Aluminum Ingots. It's the one output from this section that isn't optional: the next section's engines are built around aluminum parts."]
	quest.0A41C516E73C9C7C.subtitle: "Electrolysis, not smelting"
	quest.0A41C516E73C9C7C.title: "Aluminum"
	quest.5B185E9659A3BA80.quest_desc: ["Plastic, sulfuric acid, and electrolyzed aluminum - the Chemical Vat has gone from a curiosity to the source of half the materials in this add-on."]
	quest.5B185E9659A3BA80.subtitle: "Oil, turned into everything else"
	quest.5B185E9659A3BA80.title: "Petrochemical Industry"
	quest.3283660720DE7F6D.quest_desc: ["Each cylinder tier builds on the last: a Simple Engine Cylinder is just iron plates and flint and steel; a Diesel Engine Cylinder is aluminum plates on its own; add a Spark Plug for a full Engine Cylinder, then a Brass Pipe on top of that for the Autogas Engine Cylinder. Better cylinders accept more (and less refined) fuels."]
	quest.3283660720DE7F6D.subtitle: "Four tiers, one part"
	quest.3283660720DE7F6D.title: "Engine Cylinders"
	quest.7B82A9518004A39F.quest_desc: ["Pump air and fuel in - Diesel, Kerosene, Naphtha, or Furnace Gas - and pump carbon dioxide out through an Exhaust, and an Engine turns that into rotation through an attached shaft, the same way a Steam Engine does. Larger Radial and Turbine Engine variants exist for more power, but they all output rotation, not electricity - that's a separate machine."]
	quest.7B82A9518004A39F.subtitle: "Rotation, not electricity"
	quest.7B82A9518004A39F.title: "The Regular Engine"
	quest.01504D349B6B1195.quest_desc: ["Built the same way as a Steel Mechanism: Sequenced Assembly starting from a Shaft, deploying a Capacitor, a Steel Plate, then winding a Copper Spool onto it in a Winding Machine, then deploying a Magnet and a Steel Mechanism, 3 loops. Attach the finished Generator to a spinning shaft - an Engine's, for instance - and it starts producing real electricity: Voltage and Power."]
	quest.01504D349B6B1195.subtitle: "Rotation into electricity"
	quest.01504D349B6B1195.title: "The Generator"
	quest.25A6F89E66B3C3D5.quest_desc: ["Electric Posts (and Cable Hubs, in five metal tiers) are the physical anchors of a power network - but the actual cable is virtual. Right-click two Cable Insulators with a copper, aluminum, or constantan Spool to link them, the same way Create's own rope pulleys connect by right-clicking, not by placing a run of blocks."]
	quest.25A6F89E66B3C3D5.subtitle: "Wiring it all together"
	quest.25A6F89E66B3C3D5.title: "Posts and Cables"
	quest.5FCCEC092582A22E.quest_desc: ["Fit a Transformer with 2 Electromagnetic Coils of different turn counts and it changes voltage by their ratio - a 50-turn input feeding a 100-turn output doubles the voltage that comes out. This is a real electrical model: every device has Voltage, Current, and Resistance, and devices wired into the same numbered Group split voltage between them based on resistance. The Configuration Wrench changes which group a device belongs to."]
	quest.5FCCEC092582A22E.subtitle: "Changing voltage by turn ratio"
	quest.5FCCEC092582A22E.title: "The Transformer"
	quest.0F9D1CA729107017.quest_desc: ["A lead-acid Accumulator (lead plates and Sulfuric Acid) or a lithium-ion one (a block of Lithium and nickel plates) both produce the same battery block: charge goes in the bottom, and comes back out the top slowly. A convenience, not a requirement."]
	quest.0F9D1CA729107017.subtitle: "A battery, either way"
	quest.0F9D1CA729107017.title: "The Accumulator"
	quest.5DD23DE1046BAD7E.quest_desc: ["An Engine spinning a Generator, wired through Posts and a Transformer - electricity here isn't a flat number, it's Voltage, Current, and Resistance behaving like a real circuit."]
	quest.5DD23DE1046BAD7E.subtitle: "A real power grid"
	quest.5DD23DE1046BAD7E.title: "Electrified"
	quest.0E51508739235558.quest_desc: ["Feed the same Blast Furnace that would otherwise make Steel a stack of Quartz instead, and it produces Liquid Silicon - the reason it was worth building back in the Steel Age. Cast that in your Casting Basin for Silicon Ingots."]
	quest.0E51508739235558.subtitle: "The Blast Furnace, repurposed"
	quest.0E51508739235558.title: "Silicon"
	quest.7C68B40E85CF6677.quest_desc: ["Mix Silicon with Sulfur Dust for an N-Semiconductor, or with Aluminum for a P-Semiconductor - both plain Mechanical Mixer recipes, no vat or heat required. Together they're the guts of every transistor built from here on."]
	quest.7C68B40E85CF6677.subtitle: "N-type and P-type"
	quest.7C68B40E85CF6677.title: "Semiconductors"
	quest.7A768468706EF3C7.quest_desc: ["Plastic Sheet and green dye press into an Empty Circuit Board. A Deployer coats it with a Gold Plate for a Coated Circuit Board. A bath in Sulfuric Acid inside a Chemical Vat etches it. Finally, Sequenced Assembly deploys a Capacitor, a Resistor, a Transistor, and a second Resistor onto it, 4 loops, for a finished Circuit Board - the component nearly every advanced machine in this add-on needs at least one of."]
	quest.7A768468706EF3C7.subtitle: "Four stages, start to finish"
	quest.7A768468706EF3C7.title: "The Circuit Board"
	quest.725D2A9697073911.quest_desc: ["2 Nickel Ingots, a Silicon Ingot, and 2 Steel Ingots, mixed with heat, produce Magnetic Alloy Ingots - a genuine convergence of TFC's own nickel and steel with this add-on's silicon. An optional branch: press it into sheets for Transformers, or continue below for actual Magnets and Coils."]
	quest.725D2A9697073911.subtitle: "Nickel, silicon, and steel together"
	quest.725D2A9697073911.title: "Magnetic Alloy"
	quest.3A2EDAA6D9EEAC38.quest_desc: ["A Polarizer turns a Magnetic Alloy Ingot into a Magnet by right-clicking it in, powered, after a short wait. A Winding Machine winds a Copper Spool onto an unfinished coil (steel nuggets around a Magnetic Alloy Ingot) for an Electromagnetic Coil - both feed into motors, transformers, and the Generator itself."]
	quest.3A2EDAA6D9EEAC38.subtitle: "What a Polarizer and Winding Machine are for"
	quest.3A2EDAA6D9EEAC38.title: "Magnets and Coils"
	quest.2A2341354E9F1220.quest_desc: ["Silicon repurposed from the same Blast Furnace that was built for steel, semiconductors mixed from it, and a full Circuit Board assembled start to finish - the electronics tier is complete."]
	quest.2A2341354E9F1220.subtitle: "From sand to circuit boards"
	quest.2A2341354E9F1220.title: "Electronics, Ready"
	quest.4E03EB121ED15E32.quest_desc: ["Oil, electricity, and circuit boards - the spine of this add-on is done, built around the Steel and Cast Iron TFC already gave you. It goes much further from here: napalm and thermite weapons, upgraded potato cannons, dozens of concrete and caution-block colors for factory floors, and a whole separate ponder tutorial on Create-style fluid pipes, pumps, and valves this chapter didn't need to cover since Create Fundamentals already taught the basics. Worth exploring in-world whenever you're ready."]
	quest.4E03EB121ED15E32.subtitle: "The factory, still growing"
	quest.4E03EB121ED15E32.title: "Onward"

	quest.36619116E6F1FA81.quest_desc: [
		"The Factory Must Grow's Generator ran on Voltage and Power in the abstract. Power Grid goes further: it simulates a real electrical circuit - Voltage, Current, and Resistance obeying Ohm's Law, closed loops, resistive losses in wires, even overcurrent damage."
		""
		"The two systems aren't islands: Power Grid's Device Connector can bridge straight into a TFMG line (and into plain Forge Energy) - this is a real, developer-built compatibility feature, not a coincidence."
	]
	quest.36619116E6F1FA81.subtitle: "A second electrical system, built on real physics"
	quest.36619116E6F1FA81.title: "Welcome to Create: Power Grid"
	quest.7ECEDA5ADAB4370C.quest_desc: [
		"Cut a Copper Plate with a Mechanical Saw for 4 Wire. Wiring isn't a placed block - select one connector, then right-click a second one to link them, consuming wire based on the distance between them. A Wire Connector (Andesite Alloy plus copper nuggets) is just a routing point with no other function."
		""
		"Current only flows around a complete closed loop, and every wire has resistance - the longer the run, the more voltage is lost to heat, and too much current through too thin a wire can overheat and break it."
	]
	quest.7ECEDA5ADAB4370C.subtitle: "Right-click to link, not place-a-cable"
	quest.7ECEDA5ADAB4370C.title: "Wire and Connectors"
	quest.2E95EF4A43F16EE5.quest_desc: ["Iron plates, a zinc plate, paper, and a copper plate make a Capacitor - a small breadboard component that stores a little electricity, not a bulk battery."]
	quest.2E95EF4A43F16EE5.subtitle: "A small store of charge"
	quest.2E95EF4A43F16EE5.title: "The Capacitor"
	quest.58461B46723A481E.quest_desc: ["Deploy Andesite Alloy with copper and zinc plates for a Device Connector - the attachment point for devices that don't expose their own electrical terminals directly. It also converts to Forge Energy and to a Factory Must Grow line automatically, at a real conversion rate (shown in its tooltip), if either is installed."]
	quest.58461B46723A481E.subtitle: "The bridge to everything else"
	quest.58461B46723A481E.title: "The Device Connector"
	quest.5E006AAB8CD9501B.quest_desc: [
		"A Power Grid generator has two halves: a Stator (Copper Coils - made by right-clicking two shafts with a coil item, not placed as blocks) that creates a magnetic field, and an Armature (Rotor, Commutator, and Clutch) where electricity actually gets induced. Feed the stator a small Excitation Current through a Device Connector to start it, then spin the whole assembly with any Create rotational power source."
		""
		"A Generator Clutch (Create's Clutch plus Andesite Alloy) provides a weak, redstone-adjustable coupling between your kinetic network and the generator shaft - build one alongside the Induction Rotor, Commutator, and Housing that make up the rest of the assembly."
	]
	quest.5E006AAB8CD9501B.subtitle: "A real AC dynamo, spun by rotation"
	quest.5E006AAB8CD9501B.title: "The Generator"
	quest.4F8518D0F850B080.quest_desc: ["Sequenced Assembly on a glass pane - deploy a slime ball, then polished rose quartz, cut it, deploy a copper ingot, press it, then deploy a copper plate - for a Solar Panel. It must face the sun with a clear angle to it; obstacles, biome heat, and even glass or leaves in the way all reduce output. Its actual power follows a real solar IV curve (open-circuit voltage, short-circuit current, and a maximum-power point you match your load's resistance to) - an optional alternative to the kinetic Generator."]
	quest.4F8518D0F850B080.subtitle: "A real IV-curve, not a flat output"
	quest.4F8518D0F850B080.title: "The Solar Panel"
	quest.7DADA269F92FD78E.quest_desc: ["Mix redstone and blaze powder into heated water for Acid. Sequenced Assembly then takes a Conductive Casing (Andesite Casing plus a zinc ingot) through 3 loops - deploying a copper plate, a zinc plate, then filling with Acid - for a real lead-acid-style Battery. As it discharges, its voltage and internal resistance both drift, exactly like a real one would."]
	quest.7DADA269F92FD78E.subtitle: "Copper, zinc, and acid"
	quest.7DADA269F92FD78E.title: "The Battery"
	quest.076FB027A6BD8857.quest_desc: ["Each tier wraps the previous one in more metal: a Battery plus 8 copper ingots makes a Small Battery; a Small Battery plus 8 iron ingots makes a Medium Battery; add 8 gold ingots for a High-Voltage Battery, then 8 netherite ingots for a full Substation Battery - a real upgrade chain, each tier built directly from the last."]
	quest.076FB027A6BD8857.subtitle: "Copper, then iron, then gold, then netherite"
	quest.076FB027A6BD8857.title: "Bigger Batteries"
	quest.59D3271BB7592CA0.quest_desc: ["An LV Switch (a lever plus components) and LV Button work by hand. An MV Switch needs a copper plate instead of just components. An HV Switch is mechanically actuated by a kinetic input rather than toggled by hand - matching how a real high-voltage disconnect is never something you'd touch directly."]
	quest.59D3271BB7592CA0.subtitle: "Three voltage tiers"
	quest.59D3271BB7592CA0.title: "Switches"
	quest.02276D6D6AB924AC.quest_desc: ["Glass panes, iron plates, quartz, and iron wire make a Growth Lamp - a powered light bulb that accelerates crop growth in the area around it."]
	quest.02276D6D6AB924AC.subtitle: "Light that speeds up crops"
	quest.02276D6D6AB924AC.title: "The Growth Lamp"
	quest.5016B70D7CAC52A1.quest_desc: ["Copper plates, a Precision Mechanism, iron ingots, and a Conductive Casing make an HV Breaker - to close it, you first wind it up, then toggle it with a redstone pulse. It can be opened again without rewinding, but closing it always costs another wind."]
	quest.5016B70D7CAC52A1.subtitle: "A switch that has to be wound first"
	quest.5016B70D7CAC52A1.title: "The HV Breaker"
	quest.78A8ECDF3AEE44C7.quest_desc: ["Iron and copper plates around a Conductive Casing make a Fuse Holder - cheap insurance against the overcurrent and wire-melting damage Power Grid genuinely simulates."]
	quest.78A8ECDF3AEE44C7.subtitle: "Protection before things melt"
	quest.78A8ECDF3AEE44C7.title: "The Fuse Holder"
	quest.29572D949B702BFF.quest_desc: ["Copper Coils, a Conductive Casing, iron plates, a Magnet (Andesite Alloy run through the Magnetization process), and a Shaft assemble into an Electric Motor - the reverse of the Generator, turning electricity into rotation at a speed set by the voltage you feed it. Combine one with a Precision Mechanism for a Constant Speed Motor instead: constant speed regardless of voltage, with the voltage now setting its stress capacity and spin direction."]
	quest.29572D949B702BFF.subtitle: "Electricity back into rotation"
	quest.29572D949B702BFF.title: "The Electric Motor"
	quest.587C7CC42F506896.quest_desc: ["Six Copper Coils, a Conductive Casing, and iron plates make an Electromagnet - it holds and processes items placed or dropped on a Depot (or delivered by belt) underneath it automatically, while powered."]
	quest.587C7CC42F506896.subtitle: "Powered item sorting"
	quest.587C7CC42F506896.title: "The Electromagnet"
	quest.0C34DE4D57EE94A4.quest_desc: ["Iron plates, Pins, and 2 Resistive Coils make a Heating Coil - it heats a passing Air Flow, and enough voltage turns that into real bulk blasting heat. Built into a Basin Heater (a mechanical-crafting assembly of 5 Resistive Coils, copper plates, and a Conductive Casing) instead, the same electric heat goes straight into a Create Basin - faster processing the more voltage you push through it."]
	quest.0C34DE4D57EE94A4.subtitle: "Electric heat for bulk processing"
	quest.0C34DE4D57EE94A4.title: "Heating Coils"
	quest.0B1E3D1C92413D04.quest_desc: ["A Current Gauge, Voltage Gauge, and Power Gauge each read one value off whatever they're attached to. A Multimeter (built from a Current Gauge, a Voltage Gauge, an Electrical Gizmo, and a Conductive Casing) reads all three at once, plus resistance and the wider network's total generation and consumption - though it won't work while you're also wearing Engineer's Goggles."]
	quest.0B1E3D1C92413D04.subtitle: "Current, voltage, power, and all three at once"
	quest.0B1E3D1C92413D04.title: "Reading the Grid"
	quest.148A3705159954E0.quest_desc: ["A Resistive Coil plus coal makes a Resistor. Polished rose quartz plus a copper plate makes a Diode - power only flows out its lighter side. Sequenced Assembly on an iron plate - deploying rose quartz, then gold wire, then pressing - makes an NPN BJT, with a real chance of an in-progress PNP BJT coming out instead. All three are the actual guts of the circuit boards built next."]
	quest.148A3705159954E0.subtitle: "The parts a real circuit is built from"
	quest.148A3705159954E0.title: "Breadboard Components"
	quest.67D4FF334FCCFFD8.quest_desc: ["An Electron Tube, an empty Schematic, a Socket, Copper Plating, and a Conductive Casing make a Circuit Design Table - place traces, place components, and save the result as a schematic, the same way you'd lay out a real breadboard. There's no fixed recipe for a finished Circuit Board itself; it comes out of whatever you actually design on the table."]
	quest.67D4FF334FCCFFD8.subtitle: "A real schematic, not a fixed recipe"
	quest.67D4FF334FCCFFD8.title: "Designing a Circuit"
	quest.504E43C5B19E8B0C.quest_desc: ["Quartz, coal, an iron nugget, and a copper nugget mix (heated) into a Chip Casing. Sequenced Assembly then takes a finished Circuit Board - deploying an iron sheet, pressing it twice, then deploying the Chip Casing - into a Chip: your whole schematic, compiled down into a single component you can place on a bigger board. Chips can nest inside other chips up to a depth limit, and each chip size has its own power-dissipation ceiling."]
	quest.504E43C5B19E8B0C.subtitle: "Compiling a circuit into one component"
	quest.504E43C5B19E8B0C.title: "Chips"
	quest.26EC82A98288D97B.quest_desc: ["Copper plates and ingots make a Grounding Rod - a ground reference for your network, and genuinely worth having: excess current with nowhere else to go can damage anything standing nearby without one."]
	quest.26EC82A98288D97B.subtitle: "Where a stray charge goes instead of you"
	quest.26EC82A98288D97B.title: "The Grounding Rod"
	quest.370393D5705A47B1.quest_desc: ["Generation, storage, switching, motors, heat, measurement, and a way to design your own circuits - Power Grid's electricity behaves like the real thing from end to end, and it can still hand power straight to a Factory Must Grow line through a Device Connector whenever you need to."]
	quest.370393D5705A47B1.subtitle: "Voltage, current, and resistance, all real"
	quest.370393D5705A47B1.title: "Grid Online"
	quest.0C00047FF7F502A7.quest_desc: ["This chapter covered the spine - generation, storage, switching, and circuit design. Power Grid goes further still: string lights and modular CRT displays, a punch-card programmer, lightning attractors and grounding hazards, nether-portal-linked transformers, and an electrified baton and drill among its powered tools. All worth a look once the basics are second nature."]
	quest.0C00047FF7F502A7.subtitle: "Two electrical systems, one bridge between them"
	quest.0C00047FF7F502A7.title: "Onward"

	quest.03FC1483DAE61F9A.quest_desc: [
		"Both of these mods normally come with their own electricity systems - Mekanism's Universal Cables and generators, Immersive Engineering's LV/MV/HV lines and dynamos. Neither is craftable in this pack; Power Grid is the only electricity system here, deliberately."
		""
		"What's left is still substantial: a real ore-doubling processing chain that stacks with Create's own crushing wheel, plus a handful of genuinely non-electric machines from each mod that never needed power in the first place."
	]
	quest.03FC1483DAE61F9A.subtitle: "Processing power, not power plants"
	quest.03FC1483DAE61F9A.title: "Welcome to Mekanism and Immersive Engineering"
	quest.2C41DAA541055377.quest_desc: ["Power Grid's Device Connector converts its own electricity into Forge Energy - and an FE Inverter does the same job as a dedicated block. Either one placed against a Mekanism or Immersive Engineering machine just works: both mods accept plain Forge Energy on their power port, no mod-specific cable required."]
	quest.2C41DAA541055377.subtitle: "The same bridge, the other direction"
	quest.2C41DAA541055377.title: "Powering These Machines"
	quest.44F2756E861FF620.quest_desc: ["The Mixer, Metal Press, and Squeezer are three more of Immersive Engineering's Forge-Energy-powered machines - the same Device Connector or FE Inverter bridge from Power Grid feeds all three. Note that plate-pressing itself was removed pack-wide (TFC's anvil is the only sheet source now) - the Metal Press still handles rods, gears, and wire just fine."]
	quest.44F2756E861FF620.subtitle: "Mixing, pressing, squeezing"
	quest.44F2756E861FF620.title: "More Machines to Power"
	quest.74577891FA8723B7.quest_desc: ["Immersive Engineering's own crafting table, made from treated wood and an iron ingot - no power needed. Most of the mod's recipes are laid out on this one, not the plain vanilla grid."]
	quest.74577891FA8723B7.subtitle: "A crafting table, mostly"
	quest.74577891FA8723B7.title: "Engineer's Workbench"
	quest.46F978979273C091.quest_desc: ["A furnace, iron ingots, osmium ingots, and redstone dust - built entirely on a crafting table, no other machine required. Everything else in Mekanism's processing line runs through this first: it's the only way to make a Basic Control Circuit, which every tier-1 Mekanism machine needs."]
	quest.46F978979273C091.subtitle: "Mekanism's actual entry point"
	quest.46F978979273C091.title: "The Metallurgic Infuser"
	quest.0EAE3BEC95572246.quest_desc: ["Feed the Metallurgic Infuser redstone gas and an osmium ingot for a Basic Control Circuit. Separately, steel ingots, cheap glass, and osmium ingots make a Steel Casing. Together these two are the shared foundation under the Enrichment Chamber, Crusher, and Energized Smelter alike."]
	quest.0EAE3BEC95572246.subtitle: "What every Mekanism machine is built from"
	quest.0EAE3BEC95572246.title: "Circuits and Casings"
	quest.0A33C4C95AB03DB5.quest_desc: ["An Enrichment Chamber turns a powder or dust into 2x its next-stage counterpart - this is the machine that doubles whatever Create's own crushing wheel already produced. A Crusher does the same first step Create's wheel does, for anything that isn't part of this pack's own ore chain. An Energized Smelter is just an electric furnace - no multiplier, but automatable and immune to running out of fuel."]
	quest.0A33C4C95AB03DB5.subtitle: "Enrich, crush, and smelt - by electricity"
	quest.0A33C4C95AB03DB5.title: "Mekanism's Machines"
	quest.40935BCF9893653C.quest_desc: ["Combines items together - raw ore and cobblestone into their vanilla ore-block counterparts is its classic use, alongside a handful of other item-combining recipes."]
	quest.40935BCF9893653C.subtitle: "Raw ore plus cobblestone"
	quest.40935BCF9893653C.title: "The Combiner"
	quest.6FCF79ED902A9D95.quest_desc: ["Ore crushed by Create's own wheel, then doubled again in an Enrichment Chamber - four times what the raw ore alone would give you. Mekanism's own processing goes much deeper from here - Purification, Injection, Crystallizing - but that whole deeper chain runs on Mekanism's own gas-handling infrastructure and isn't part of what this pack actually built around it. Worth exploring on your own if you want to push past 4x, but not required for anything ahead."]
	quest.6FCF79ED902A9D95.subtitle: "Create, then Mekanism"
	quest.6FCF79ED902A9D95.title: "4x Ore Processing"
	quest.5CB12DC6215C4943.quest_desc: ["Immersive Engineering's own Crusher mirrors every single crushing recipe Create's wheel can do, anywhere in this pack - not just ore. A genuine full alternative, not a lesser copy, if you'd rather build one machine than a wheel-and-shaft setup."]
	quest.5CB12DC6215C4943.subtitle: "An alternate to Create's wheel, pack-wide"
	quest.5CB12DC6215C4943.title: "IE's Crusher"
	quest.58EF633CC9B323D7.quest_desc: ["Feed an actual Enrichment Chamber into the recipe and you get a Basic Enriching Factory back - the same 2x doubling, run on several items in parallel instead of one at a time. A genuine upgrade, not a separate machine."]
	quest.58EF633CC9B323D7.subtitle: "The Enrichment Chamber, multiplied"
	quest.58EF633CC9B323D7.title: "The Enriching Factory"
	quest.01C2E7E00E635E4F.quest_desc: ["A string, an iron ingot, and a wooden rod. Every Immersive Engineering multiblock - the Arc Furnace included - starts as component blocks placed in the right shape, then right-clicked with this to lock them together into a working machine."]
	quest.01C2E7E00E635E4F.subtitle: "What turns a pile of blocks into a machine"
	quest.01C2E7E00E635E4F.title: "Engineer's Hammer"
	quest.6AEE3DC80ACB73CB.quest_desc: ["Build the structure, then seal it with an Engineer's Hammer. Fed with the dust or clump an Enrichment Chamber already doubled, the Arc Furnace doubles it again - 8x the original ore, the top of this pack's own ore-processing chain. It also has empty additive slots for real alloying recipes elsewhere in the mod, and produces Slag as a byproduct - not waste, it presses into Slag Bricks or crushes down into Slag Gravel."]
	quest.6AEE3DC80ACB73CB.subtitle: "The last stage of this ore chain"
	quest.6AEE3DC80ACB73CB.title: "The Arc Furnace"
	quest.6EFB95F24D0C0BDD.quest_desc: ["Crushed, enriched, and arc-smelted - three mods' worth of processing stacked on the same ore, for eight times what digging it up alone would give you."]
	quest.6EFB95F24D0C0BDD.subtitle: "Create, Mekanism, and Immersive Engineering"
	quest.6EFB95F24D0C0BDD.title: "8x Ore Processing"
	quest.1356D06D154F51AC.quest_desc: ["Immersive Engineering ships its own Coke Oven, running on the same coal briquettes this pack already retargeted The Factory Must Grow's Coke Oven to use - the two are genuinely parallel, not in conflict, if you'd rather build one over the other."]
	quest.1356D06D154F51AC.subtitle: "A second coke oven, same fuel"
	quest.1356D06D154F51AC.title: "IE's Coke Oven"
	quest.6C45FF8565A7EFD4.quest_desc: ["Unlike almost everything else in this chapter, the Alloy Smelter runs on heat and fuel alone - no Forge Energy required. It alloys metals together directly, the same job a TFC crucible does, just through a different machine."]
	quest.6C45FF8565A7EFD4.subtitle: "No power needed for this one"
	quest.6C45FF8565A7EFD4.title: "The Alloy Smelter"
	quest.2F5F3DDB0055E37E.quest_desc: ["Also entirely fuel-based, no electricity - coal coke or charcoal heats iron into steel here, alongside Slag as a byproduct. Worth knowing this exists, since it's a second route to the same steel tier TFC's own Bloomery and Blast Furnace already produce - not something to lean on if you'd rather keep TFC's own iron progression as the one path that matters."]
	quest.2F5F3DDB0055E37E.subtitle: "A second iron-to-steel path"
	quest.2F5F3DDB0055E37E.title: "IE's Blast Furnace"
	quest.511B48DF1DED0783.quest_desc: ["Most of Immersive Engineering's wire coils lost their purpose along with the electricity network they used to connect - but Structure Rope is purely mechanical (climbable, load-bearing, nothing to do with power), and Razor Wire is a plain damage-dealing defensive trap built from treated fence and steel. Both still work exactly as intended."]
	quest.511B48DF1DED0783.subtitle: "The wire coils that still do something"
	quest.511B48DF1DED0783.title: "Rope and Razor Wire"
	chapter.596053404295DE98.subtitle: "Where to explore, what waits there"
	chapter.596053404295DE98.title: "Adventure: Exploration"

	quest.3972E5BEAD693520.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter and its companion, Boss Hunting, sit outside the main progression entirely - nothing in either one is required to reach anything in another chapter, and nothing else is required to start these. Jump in whenever exploring sounds more fun than building."
		""
		"This one covers where the pack's dungeon and structure mods actually put their content, plus the two real boss-gated dimensions in this pack: the Otherside (through the Deep Dark) and the Aether."
	]
	quest.3972E5BEAD693520.subtitle: "Nothing here gates anything else"
	quest.3972E5BEAD693520.title: "Welcome to Adventure: Exploration"
	quest.701FF404402732AD.quest_desc: ["Yung's Better Dungeons, Mineshafts, Nether Fortresses, Strongholds, Ocean Monuments, and Better End Island each fully redesign the named vanilla structure into something bigger and more varied - they replace the vanilla version outright rather than adding alongside it. A dedicated compat mod makes Better Dungeons generate correctly across TFC's own custom biomes."]
	quest.701FF404402732AD.subtitle: "Complete redesigns, not additions"
	quest.701FF404402732AD.title: "Yung's Structures"
	quest.7A13DE2877A91428.quest_desc: ["Moog's Mineshafts Reimagined, Nether Structures, Temples Reimagined, Voyager Structures, and End Structures add genuinely new structures built from vanilla blocks, rather than replacing anything - Voyager Structures alone adds well over a hundred village and ruin variants across every biome."]
	quest.7A13DE2877A91428.subtitle: "New content, not redesigns"
	quest.7A13DE2877A91428.title: "Moog's Structures"
	quest.3C0A13FEA6CB5385.quest_desc: ["TFC Ruins adds its own basement, beach, rich, and small ruin variants. TFC Ancient City brings the vanilla Ancient City into TFC's own mountain and plateau biomes, with its key blocks aligned to TFC's equivalents instead of feeling out of place."]
	quest.3C0A13FEA6CB5385.subtitle: "Purpose-built for this world"
	quest.3C0A13FEA6CB5385.title: "TFC's Own Ruins"
	quest.0B73C3EBE1E9CD6B.quest_desc: ["Beneath reworks the Nether itself into something styled after TFC, not a separate dimension. To open the way: hold a Scythe, gather 7 offerings near an Ancient Altar (skulls, anvils, placed gold, pig iron, or black steel), then kill a pig, goat, or sheep within 5 blocks of them - the portal opens and briefly reaches into the overworld."]
	quest.0B73C3EBE1E9CD6B.subtitle: "A ritual, not a portal frame"
	quest.0B73C3EBE1E9CD6B.title: "Opening the Beneath"
	quest.63899A598B23CE27.quest_desc: ["Nether Gold, Nether Pyrite, Blackstone Sylvite, and Nether Cursecoal are new ore types; Ghost Pepper, Gleamflower, and Crimson/Warped Roots are new crops. A Hellforge acts as a heat source down here. There's no dedicated boss waiting for you - the real danger is the Lost Page tome-gambling mechanic, which can curse you with a buffed Wither Skeleton champion if your luck runs out."]
	quest.63899A598B23CE27.subtitle: "New ores, new crops, real risk"
	quest.63899A598B23CE27.title: "What Waits in the Beneath"
	quest.669413BD9E408B7D.quest_desc: ["The path into the Otherside runs through the vanilla Deep Dark - find an Ancient City, and kill the Warden guarding it. Nothing about the Warden itself is changed here; it's the gate, not the destination."]
	quest.669413BD9E408B7D.subtitle: "The Deep Dark's own guardian, unchanged"
	quest.669413BD9E408B7D.title: "The Warden"
	quest.2E8C0C919AEEBEA1.quest_desc: ["Beyond the Warden, an Otherside Portal opens a real second dimension with four biomes of its own: Deeplands, Echoing Forest, Blooming Caverns, and Overcast Columns."]
	quest.2E8C0C919AEEBEA1.subtitle: "A whole second dimension"
	quest.2E8C0C919AEEBEA1.title: "Into the Otherside"
	quest.5A69820872D67BBF.quest_desc: ["Somewhere in the Otherside stands an Ancient Temple - the destination structure, and where the area's toughest resident is waiting."]
	quest.5A69820872D67BBF.subtitle: "What you came here to find"
	quest.5A69820872D67BBF.title: "The Ancient Temple"
	quest.1A5BE1CC7A8301DD.quest_desc: ["200 health, a Warden-style vibration-sensing ambush, and the Ancient Temple as its home turf - the Stalker is the real test of this whole area, well above anything else living in the Otherside."]
	quest.1A5BE1CC7A8301DD.subtitle: "The Otherside's apex predator"
	quest.1A5BE1CC7A8301DD.title: "The Stalker"
	quest.034F4F9B29CD9901.quest_desc: ["A Phantom, a second Warden, an Angler Fish, a Sculk Centipede, a Sculk Leech, a Sculk Snapper, a Shattered, and a Shriek Worm - the Otherside's full mob roster, one confirmed kill each."]
	quest.034F4F9B29CD9901.subtitle: "A full roster, one at a time"
	quest.034F4F9B29CD9901.title: "Every Sculk Mob"
	quest.5D2742B2341907BC.quest_desc: ["The Aether is its own sky dimension with three named dungeons, each gated behind killing the boss guarding the one before it - Bronze, then Silver, then Gold. This pack's Deep Aether add-on inserts a fourth dungeon, Brass, parallel to Bronze rather than after it."]
	quest.5D2742B2341907BC.subtitle: "A sky dimension with a real boss ladder"
	quest.5D2742B2341907BC.title: "Reaching the Aether"
	quest.541C7DC123DAADCF.quest_desc: ["The first of the Aether's three main dungeons. Slider guards it: 400 health, and it fights by charging and colliding rather than a conventional melee attack."]
	quest.541C7DC123DAADCF.subtitle: "Slider"
	quest.541C7DC123DAADCF.title: "The Bronze Dungeon"
	quest.0292B80C24DD4251.quest_desc: ["Deep Aether's own addition, sitting alongside Bronze rather than after it. The Eye of the Storm is a segmented flying boss - a 220-health controller plus many 10-health body segments, each one a separate hittable part - languishing in the sky above the dungeon."]
	quest.0292B80C24DD4251.subtitle: "Eye of the Storm"
	quest.0292B80C24DD4251.title: "The Brass Dungeon"
	quest.3779CEED5DDBE3FB.quest_desc: ["Opens once Slider is down. The Valkyrie Queen guards it: 500 health, 13.5 attack, and a full escort of lesser Valkyries."]
	quest.3779CEED5DDBE3FB.subtitle: "Valkyrie Queen"
	quest.3779CEED5DDBE3FB.title: "The Silver Dungeon"
	quest.478AD913394258CA.quest_desc: ["The last of the Aether's three main dungeons, opened after the Valkyrie Queen falls. The Sun Spirit guards it: 500 health, and it fights entirely at range with fire, backed by Fire Minions."]
	quest.478AD913394258CA.subtitle: "Sun Spirit"
	quest.478AD913394258CA.title: "The Gold Dungeon"
	quest.64EE5A3DA9734BDC.quest_desc: ["The real capstone: kill Slider, the Eye of the Storm, the Valkyrie Queen, and the Sun Spirit each without taking damage in the fight. A genuine mastery challenge, not just a checklist."]
	quest.64EE5A3DA9734BDC.subtitle: "All four, without taking a hit"
	quest.64EE5A3DA9734BDC.title: "Aether Champion"
	quest.2954152D6719E018.quest_desc: ["The Otherside cleared, the Aether's three dungeons down, Deep Aether's fourth alongside them - between all of these mods' own structures, there's no shortage of somewhere left to dig, sail, or fly to next."]
	quest.2954152D6719E018.subtitle: "There's always another structure"
	quest.2954152D6719E018.title: "Exploration, For Now"
	chapter.3CB10A29BFFFDBD5.subtitle: "A real difficulty order, across four different mods"
	chapter.3CB10A29BFFFDBD5.title: "Adventure: Boss Hunting"

	quest.1AB6DAFE4883C4E9.quest_desc: [
		"Cataclysm, Ice and Fire, Legendary Monsters, and Bosses of Mass Destruction each add their own boss roster, with no shared sense of how they compare to each other. This chapter orders all of them together by their actual health pools - the one stat every one of these mods exposes - grouped into Early, Mid, and Late tiers, with two true apex fights at the very end."
		""
		"This whole chapter sits outside the main progression - nothing here is required to reach anything else, and nothing else is required to start it."
	]
	quest.1AB6DAFE4883C4E9.subtitle: "One difficulty order, four different mods"
	quest.1AB6DAFE4883C4E9.title: "Welcome to Boss Hunting"
	quest.454F822C907BE2F6.quest_desc: ["Apotheosis adds a real gear-upgrade path worth knowing about before diving into any of this: Affixes and Gems that socket into weapons and armor, a Reforging Station to re-roll them, and Gateways - a roguelike dungeon with four difficulty tiers of its own (Ascent, Frontier, Summit, Pinnacle) - as a way to farm better gear before you go looking for any of the bosses below."]
	quest.454F822C907BE2F6.subtitle: "Apotheosis exists"
	quest.454F822C907BE2F6.title: "Before You Start"
	quest.0651450D45B5BF4F.quest_desc: ["Ignited Revenant, Ender Golem, and Clawdian - three lighter fights (80-225 health) that Cataclysm itself gates its three toughest bosses behind. Beat these first; each one unlocks the real fight standing behind it."]
	quest.0651450D45B5BF4F.subtitle: "Cataclysm's own warm-up fights"
	quest.0651450D45B5BF4F.title: "Early Tier: The Precursors"
	quest.59F835CA7C9A5F66.quest_desc: ["Ancient Guardian, Overgrown Colossus, and Dune Sentinel - three 170-health bosses guarding an Ancient Stronghold, a Mossy Temple, and a Ruined Pyramid respectively. The Ancient Guardian hits harder than its health suggests - 20 attack damage, the highest raw attack found anywhere in this whole tier list."]
	quest.59F835CA7C9A5F66.subtitle: "Legendary Monsters' entry point"
	quest.59F835CA7C9A5F66.title: "Early Tier: Overworld Dungeons"
	quest.55B4411056C7CBF5.quest_desc: ["Lava Eater and Skeletosaurus (both 170-200 health, Legendary Monsters), Withered Abomination (190, also Legendary Monsters), and the Nether Gauntlet (250, Bosses of Mass Destruction, drops Ancient Debris on death) - round out the early tier before the real difficulty jump."]
	quest.55B4411056C7CBF5.subtitle: "Four more, before moving up"
	quest.55B4411056C7CBF5.title: "Early Tier: Nether Fights"
	quest.500DDE8060189322.quest_desc: ["Void Blossom (350, an Overworld glass cannon - low armor but the highest health of BOMD's four), Night Lich (300, forces night and summons an undead army), and Obsidilith (300, found in The End). All three regenerate health if you don't keep the pressure on."]
	quest.500DDE8060189322.subtitle: "All four idle-heal if you stall"
	quest.500DDE8060189322.title: "Mid Tier: Bosses of Mass Destruction"
	quest.7C61C07ECF367EFE.quest_desc: ["Ender Guardian (333 health, the highest armor of any boss surveyed here - 20), The Harbinger (390, fights entirely at range), and Scylla (390, the Storm Empress) - the fights Ender Golem and Clawdian were standing in front of."]
	quest.7C61C07ECF367EFE.subtitle: "What the precursors were guarding"
	quest.7C61C07ECF367EFE.title: "Mid Tier: Cataclysm, Part One"
	quest.7DB4BA891D03A8DB.quest_desc: ["The Leviathan (400, only vulnerable while in water - fight it in the Sunken City), Maledictus (420, Frosted Prison), Ignis (450, Burning Arena, the fight Ignited Revenant was guarding), and Ancient Remnant (450, Cursed Pyramid) - Cataclysm's four mid-tier structures, each with its own boss."]
	quest.7DB4BA891D03A8DB.subtitle: "Four structures, four fights"
	quest.7DB4BA891D03A8DB.title: "Mid Tier: Cataclysm, Part Two"
	quest.42E4ADF5EEBDF21A.quest_desc: ["Chorusent (200, Ancient Tower Remains), Shulker Mimic (200, Shulker Tower), Annihilation Pursuer (210, deep in the Space Station chain), Cloud Golem (350, Cloudy Temple - the actual boss version, not the lesser Cumulonimbus mob that shares part of its name), and Frostbitten Golem (220, Frostbitten Temple)."]
	quest.42E4ADF5EEBDF21A.subtitle: "Five fights, five different structures"
	quest.42E4ADF5EEBDF21A.title: "Mid Tier: Legendary Monsters, The Deep End"
	quest.27DE5EB560B79121.quest_desc: ["600 health - the single highest of anything Cataclysm has to offer, found via the Soul Black Smith in the Nether. Its sustained damage output is also the highest of any Cataclysm boss."]
	quest.27DE5EB560B79121.subtitle: "Cataclysm's toughest"
	quest.27DE5EB560B79121.title: "Late Tier: Netherite Monstrosity"
	quest.0EB9D03DD4BAE985.quest_desc: ["Possessed Paladin (400, the end of the Abandoned Crypt chain) clears the way to The Obliterator (450) - found at the Space Station, six advancement-tiers deep into the End branch, with an elaborate teleport-grab and bomb-throwing moveset that makes its raw stats undersell the fight. This is Legendary Monsters' own intended final boss."]
	quest.0EB9D03DD4BAE985.subtitle: "Legendary Monsters' actual final boss"
	quest.0EB9D03DD4BAE985.title: "Late Tier: The Obliterator"
	quest.1027B166EA5BCFC2.quest_desc: ["Ice and Fire's three elemental dragons, each capping out around 500 health as adults, with their own elemental bonus damage on top of a shared 17 base attack. Each nests in its own Cave and Roost structure pair - hunt an adult of each color."]
	quest.1027B166EA5BCFC2.subtitle: "Fire, Ice, and Lightning"
	quest.1027B166EA5BCFC2.title: "Late Tier: The Dragons"
	quest.1AE10373EBE7DAB0.quest_desc: ["750 health and 30 armor - both the highest of anything surveyed across all four boss mods in this pack, by a clear margin. This is the real final fight, not a formality after the dragons."]
	quest.1AE10373EBE7DAB0.subtitle: "The single toughest fight in this chapter"
	quest.1AE10373EBE7DAB0.title: "Apex: The Dread Queen"
	quest.49634CD032DDA4F4.quest_desc: ["Every named boss across four different mods, roughly ordered by how much health stands between you and the kill. Health alone doesn't capture everything - damage caps, multi-phase attacks, and sheer moveset complexity all matter too - but it's the one number every one of these mods actually exposes, and it got you here."]
	quest.49634CD032DDA4F4.subtitle: "There's always a harder fight somewhere"
	quest.49634CD032DDA4F4.title: "Hunt Complete"
	chapter.12A0CB238126E034.title: "Iron's Spellbooks"
	chapter.12A0CB238126E034.subtitle: "Robes, runes, and two real bosses"
	quest.017192D0C1FA6DF3.title: "Welcome to Iron's Spellbooks"
	quest.017192D0C1FA6DF3.subtitle: "Magic sits outside the main progression too"
	quest.017192D0C1FA6DF3.quest_desc: [
		"Iron's Spellbooks adds a full spellcasting progression on the side: Spell Books, school-themed robes, staffs, and its own dungeons. Like the rest of the Adventure chapters, nothing here is required to reach anything else, and nothing else is required to start it."
		""
		"The path below: pick up the basic stations, get your first Spell Book, pick a school and gear up, then work your way through the Catacombs and the Citadel to two real bosses."
	]
	quest.5F5C5603449D3E0E.title: "The Inscription Table"
	quest.5F5C5603449D3E0E.subtitle: "Where every spellcaster starts"
	quest.5F5C5603449D3E0E.quest_desc: [
		"A cheap first station - wooden slabs, wooden fences, and a book. The Inscription Table is where a Scroll gets inscribed into a Spell Book, so it's the very first thing to build."
	]
	quest.0BFD46C47F4EB529.title: "The Scroll Forge"
	quest.0BFD46C47F4EB529.subtitle: "Turns Ink into Scrolls"
	quest.0BFD46C47F4EB529.quest_desc: [
		"Built from polished deepslate and crying obsidian. The Scroll Forge turns Ink into a Scroll, which the Inscription Table then reads into a Spell Book. Higher-rarity Scrolls need a higher-tier Spell Book to accept them - a Flimsy Journal can't hold what an Ancient Codex can."
	]
	quest.29493AE0584772AC.title: "The Arcane Anvil"
	quest.29493AE0584772AC.subtitle: "Upgrade Orbs and Imbuements go here"
	quest.29493AE0584772AC.quest_desc: [
		"Crafted from amethyst blocks, a diamond, an anvil, and polished deepslate. The Arcane Anvil applies Upgrade Orbs and Imbuements to gear and Spell Books - and a Shriving Stone used on it strips an Imbuement or Upgrade back off again."
	]
	quest.52B6243D28BDBEEB.title: "Your First Spell Book"
	quest.52B6243D28BDBEEB.subtitle: "Flimsy Journal to Ancient Codex"
	quest.52B6243D28BDBEEB.quest_desc: [
		"Spell Books scale with material tier, same order as vanilla tools: Copper (Flimsy Journal) -> Iron (Ironbound Tome) -> Gold (Apprentice's Spell Book) -> Diamond (Enchanted Spell Book) -> Netherite (Ancient Codex). Start with a Copper Spell Book from copper ingots, paper, and string."
		""
		"Ink for Scrolls has its own five-tier chain at the Alchemist Cauldron: Common -> (+copper ingot) -> Uncommon -> (+iron ingot) -> Rare -> (+gold ingot) -> Epic -> (+amethyst) -> Legendary. A book can only accept a Scroll at or below its own rarity tier, so the Ink chain and the Spell Book chain need to be climbed together."
	]
	quest.31BF36845FE09971.title: "Wizard Robes"
	quest.31BF36845FE09971.subtitle: "The base every school set is built from"
	quest.31BF36845FE09971.quest_desc: [
		"Crafted from Magic Cloth. Wizard Robes are the tier-0 base that every one of the eight school armor sets - Pyromancer, Cryomancer, Electromancer, Priest, Shadow-Walker, Cultist, Archevoker, and Plagued - gets upgraded from."
	]
	quest.75BF3DBB480018AA.title: "Pick a School"
	quest.75BF3DBB480018AA.subtitle: "Eight runes, eight schools"
	quest.75BF3DBB480018AA.quest_desc: [
		"Eight Spell Schools have a full gear line, each behind its own Rune: Fire -> Fire Rune, Ice -> Ice Rune, Lightning -> Lightning Rune, Holy -> Holy Rune, Ender -> Ender Rune, Blood -> Blood Rune, Evocation -> Evocation Rune, Nature -> Nature Rune. Combine a Rune with Wizard Robes (shapeless, or on a smithing table) to upgrade them into that school's armor set."
		""
		"Two more schools exist - Void and Eldritch - but neither has a Rune, an Upgrade Orb, or an armor set. Eldritch is learned separately from an Eldritch Manuscript (ancient knowledge fragments and an echo shard)."
	]
	quest.102F950AB588E6B7.title: "School Armor"
	quest.102F950AB588E6B7.subtitle: "Pyromancer Robe shown here, same pattern for all eight"
	quest.102F950AB588E6B7.quest_desc: [
		"A full school set - Pyromancer Robe pictured, but the same Rune-upgrade recipe applies to any of the eight schools - grants one extra spell slot per piece worn once the full set is on."
	]
	quest.16ED6F3090986798.title: "A Basic Staff"
	quest.16ED6F3090986798.subtitle: "Graybeard, Ice, or Artificer's Cane"
	quest.16ED6F3090986798.quest_desc: [
		"Three staffs are craftable from the start: the Graybeard Staff (cheapest - a wooden shovel, iron, and arcane essence), the Ice Staff (a Frosted Helve and a Permafrost Shard), and the Artificer's Cane (amethyst, crimson planks, and gold). A fourth, The Blood Staff, isn't craftable at all - it only drops from the Dead King."
	]
	quest.580760B3BDA8A427.title: "Spell Slots and Attributes"
	quest.580760B3BDA8A427.subtitle: "More slots, more power"
	quest.580760B3BDA8A427.quest_desc: [
		"A Lesser Spell Slot Improvement (Magic Cloth and Hogskin) raises how many spells a Spell Book can hold, independent of armor. Iron's Spellbooks also adds its own attributes worth watching - Max Mana, Mana Regeneration, Spell Power, Cast Time and Cooldown Reduction, plus separate Magic Resistance and Spell Power per school."
	]
	quest.6DA1C6AB02B87073.title: "The Wayward Compass"
	quest.6DA1C6AB02B87073.subtitle: "Points toward the Catacombs"
	quest.6DA1C6AB02B87073.quest_desc: [
		"Crafted from arcane essence, iron, and a soul lantern. The Wayward Compass points toward the nearest Catacombs - the dungeon that guards the Dead King."
	]
	quest.3BEF947B1CD7566E.title: "Into the Catacombs"
	quest.3BEF947B1CD7566E.subtitle: "Bone Keys unlock its vaults"
	quest.3BEF947B1CD7566E.quest_desc: [
		"Follow the compass into the Catacombs. Bone Keys found while exploring unlock its vaults - collect what you can on the way to the Throne Room at its heart."
	]
	quest.50BA79366F2A45A9.title: "The Dead King"
	quest.50BA79366F2A45A9.subtitle: "The Catacombs' boss"
	quest.50BA79366F2A45A9.quest_desc: [
		"Waits in the Catacombs' Throne Room."
	]
	quest.723A36876DF94EC4.title: "The King's Spoils"
	quest.723A36876DF94EC4.subtitle: "Blood Staff or Necronomicon"
	quest.723A36876DF94EC4.quest_desc: [
		"The Dead King has a real chance to drop either The Blood Staff or the Necronomicon Spell Book - both otherwise uncraftable. He also leaves behind a Dead King Soul: collect Phylactery Shards, craft a new Phylactery at a Soul Lantern, and use it on the Soul to fight him again."
	]
	quest.1E85EA59DC347EA4.title: "Furled Map: The Citadel"
	quest.1E85EA59DC347EA4.subtitle: "Cinder Essence and Ancient Knowledge"
	quest.1E85EA59DC347EA4.quest_desc: [
		"Crafted from Cinder Essence and an Ancient Knowledge Fragment. This map leads to the Citadel - home to a second real boss and a tough elite guard."
	]
	quest.05706416D08D95A0.title: "Echo of Tyros, First Flamebearer"
	quest.05706416D08D95A0.subtitle: "The Citadel's true boss"
	quest.05706416D08D95A0.quest_desc: [
		"The Citadel's real boss fight. Always drops a Divine Soulshard - the ingredient both endgame capstone chestplates need - plus a chance at the Decrepit Scythe or the Betrayer's Signet."
	]
	quest.49CED4C2B3416CD9.title: "The Ancient Knight"
	quest.49CED4C2B3416CD9.subtitle: "Guards the Citadel's vaults (optional)"
	quest.49CED4C2B3416CD9.quest_desc: [
		"Not a full boss fight - the Ancient Knight has no boss bar of its own - but it's a tough elite guarding the Citadel's Decrepit Keys and vaults. Worth clearing for the loot: guaranteed Cinder Essence, with a real chance at Netherite Scrap."
	]
	quest.7C49618CC499FFF8.title: "Mithril Weave"
	quest.7C49618CC499FFF8.subtitle: "TFC mithril, not the mod's own scrap"
	quest.7C49618CC499FFF8.quest_desc: [
		"Iron's Spellbooks' own Mithril Scrap has been redirected in this pack to require a TFC-cast Mithril Sheet instead (Mithril is a TFC/TFCM metal, epic rarity, found through Create's ore prospecting). Mithril Weave itself skips that redirect entirely though - it's a straight 3x3 recipe of a TFC Mithril Ingot and a Chain, and it's the material both capstone chestplates below are built around."
	]
	quest.7BACF52EF0EB31F0.title: "Lightbringer Chestplate"
	quest.7BACF52EF0EB31F0.subtitle: "Priest Robe + Divine Soulshard + Mithril Weave"
	quest.7BACF52EF0EB31F0.quest_desc: [
		"One of two true capstone chestplates in this mod. The Lightbringer Chestplate upgrades a Priest Chestplate with a Divine Soulshard, Mithril Weave, and gold. The other, the Infernal Sorcerer Chestplate, follows the same pattern from a Pyromancer Chestplate but swaps the gold for Pyrium."
	]
	quest.7188DDBF1E752EBE.title: "A Complete Spellcaster"
	quest.7188DDBF1E752EBE.subtitle: "Every school, both bosses, both keys"
	quest.7188DDBF1E752EBE.quest_desc: [
		"A full loadout: a school armor set with real spell slots, a staff, and a capstone chestplate built from a boss drop. Like the rest of this pack's Adventure content, none of it was required to get here - and nothing past this point needs it either."
	]
}
